window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b061-259c9a48476d4b16.json"]={sha256:"259c9a48476d4b16d14f6b2ff5cd548b6a2b08620f39126364e9caa639853388",value:{"id":"b061","title":"高層建築核心筒滑模施工","titleEn":"Slipform construction of high-rise cores","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"滑模把核心筒牆體當成一條不停的生產線：約 1.2 m 高的模板由千斤頂沿爬桿每隔數分鐘上升一小段，下緣出模的混凝土必須已能自立，上方同時綁紮鋼筋、安裝埋件並澆置。本課以 CN Tower、ThyssenKrupp 羅特魏爾試驗塔與亞特蘭大電梯試驗塔為例，說明滑升速度與凝結時間、爬桿挫屈、埋件協調、垂直度與扭轉控制、冷縫與養護、以及竣工紀錄。","summaryEn":"Slipforming turns a core wall into a non-stop production line: forms about 1.2 m high are jacked up rods a small step every few minutes, concrete leaving the bottom edge must already stand on its own, and above it crews fix rebar, set embeds and place concrete at the same time. Using the CN Tower, the ThyssenKrupp test tower in Rottweil and the elevator test tower in Atlanta, the course covers slip rate versus setting time, climbing-rod buckling, embed coordination, verticality and twist control, cold joints and curing, and as-built records.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-concrete-steel","subcategoryTitle":"混凝土與鋼構施工技術","subcategoryTitleEn":"Concrete and steel construction technology","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-concrete-steel","learningTags":["structures","st-concrete-steel","concrete"],"architectureFamily":"concrete","architectureNodes":[["核心筒牆體","Core walls"],["滑動模板與軛架","Sliding forms and yokes"],["千斤頂與爬桿","Jacks and climbing rods"],["工作平台與修飾架","Working deck and finishing scaffolds"],["混凝土供應與成熟度監測","Concrete supply and maturity monitoring"],["測量與滑升日誌","Survey and slip log"]],"architectureEdges":[[1,0],[2,1],[2,0],[3,2],[4,1],[5,3],[5,0]],"diagram":{"type":"concrete","labels":["核心筒牆體","滑動模板與軛架","千斤頂與爬桿","工作平台與修飾架","混凝土供應與成熟度監測"],"labelsEn":["Core walls","Sliding forms and yokes","Jacks and climbing rods","Working deck and finishing scaffolds","Concrete supply and maturity monitoring"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"規劃練習：一座 120 m 高的核心筒，牆體總長 150 m、厚 0.4 m，以滑模施工。模板高 1.2 m、頂部預留 0.2 m，20°C 時初凝 4 h，容許速度上限 1.0/4 = 0.25 m/h，採用 0.10 m/h 保留裕度；日升 2.4 m，純滑升 120/2.4 = 50 天，加上 3 次計畫停機各 1 天，約 53 天。混凝土供應 150×0.4×0.10 = 6.0 m³/h，全程約 150×0.4×120 = 7,200 m³。平台荷重約 4,055 kN，爬桿 48.3×4 mm 在 1.5 m 無支撐長的容許荷重約 48 kN，需約 84 支千斤頂。若改在冬季施工，成熟度要求使速度降為約 0.067 m/h：純滑升 120/(0.067×24) ≈ 75 天，供料降為約 4.0 m³/h，工期增加約 25 天，但千斤頂數量不變。數值為教學假設，不代表任何實際建築的施工計畫。","textEn":"Planning exercise: a 120 m core with 150 m of wall at 0.4 m thick is slipformed. With 1.2 m forms and 0.2 m freeboard and initial set at 4 h at 20°C, the upper rate limit is 1.0/4 = 0.25 m/h, and 0.10 m/h is chosen for margin; the core rises 2.4 m a day, so sliding takes 120/2.4 = 50 days, about 53 days with three planned one-day stops. Concrete supply is 150×0.4×0.10 = 6.0 m³/h, about 150×0.4×120 = 7,200 m³ in total. Deck load is about 4,055 kN and a 48.3×4 mm rod with 1.5 m unbraced length allows about 48 kN, so about 84 jacks are needed. In winter the maturity requirement cuts the rate to about 0.067 m/h: sliding takes 120/(0.067×24) ≈ 75 days, supply falls to about 4.0 m³/h and the programme grows by about 25 days, while the number of jacks is unchanged. Values are teaching assumptions, not any real building's construction plan.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b061-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「滑模原理與核心筒的適用條件」與「凝結時間、模板高度與容許滑升速度」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Slipform principle and when cores suit it\" and \"Setting time, form height and allowable slip rate\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b061-v13-01","title":"滑模原理與核心筒的適用條件：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Slipform principle and when cores suit it: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「連續滑升工序」如何影響高層建築核心筒滑模施工的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Continuous slipform cycle” governs force, deformation or durability in “Slipform construction of high-rise cores”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"滑模是一組沿牆體全周連續的模板，由頂部工作平台與軛架連成整體，千斤頂夾住埋在牆中的爬桿往上爬，帶動模板、平台與懸吊的修飾架一起上升。混凝土在模板內停留數小時，從頂部澆入、到下緣出模時已經初凝，可以支撐自身重量。因為模板不拆不組，核心筒每天可上升數公尺，但前提是斷面在高度方向少變化、開口與埋件能在滑升中連續安裝，且全天候不中斷供料。CN Tower 的混凝土塔身就是以液壓爬升千斤頂推動的模具連續成形，並在升高過程中逐步收窄形成錐形。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「連續滑升工序」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A slipform is a continuous ring of forms around the whole wall, tied by yokes to a working deck on top; jacks grip climbing rods embedded in the wall and climb them, lifting the forms, deck and hanging finishing scaffolds together. Concrete stays in the form for several hours, entering at the top and leaving the bottom edge after initial set, able to carry its own weight. Because nothing is struck and re-erected, a core can rise several metres a day, provided the section changes little with height, openings and embeds can be installed on the move and concrete supply continues around the clock. The CN Tower's concrete shaft was formed this way by a mould driven up by hydraulic climbing jacks, narrowing gradually as it rose to form the taper. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Continuous slipform cycle” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：滑升速度 0.10 m/h、全天 24 h 連續作業時日升 2.4 m；120 m 核心筒需 120/2.4 = 50 天，若計入 10% 的停機與調整時間，約需 50/0.9 ≈ 56 天。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: At 0.10 m/h around the clock the core rises 2.4 m a day; a 120 m core takes 120/2.4 = 50 days, or about 50/0.9 ≈ 56 days allowing 10% for stoppages and adjustments.","failure":"常見誤解：「滑模適用於所有高層核心筒，只要速度夠快就一定比較省工期。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Slipforming suits every high-rise core and is always faster if the rate is high enough.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「連續滑升工序」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Continuous slipform cycle”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-01-k1","title":"滑模原理與核心筒的適用條件","titleEn":"Slipform principle and when cores suit it","text":"滑模是一組沿牆體全周連續的模板，由頂部工作平台與軛架連成整體，千斤頂夾住埋在牆中的爬桿往上爬，帶動模板、平台與懸吊的修飾架一起上升。混凝土在模板內停留數小時，從頂部澆入、到下緣出模時已經初凝，可以支撐自身重量。","textEn":"A slipform is a continuous ring of forms around the whole wall, tied by yokes to a working deck on top; jacks grip climbing rods embedded in the wall and climb them, lifting the forms, deck and hanging finishing scaffolds together. Concrete stays in the form for several hours, entering at the top and leaving the bottom edge after initial set, able to carry its own weight.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：滑模適用於所有高層核心筒，只要速度夠快就一定比較省工期。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Slipforming suits every high-rise core and is always faster if the rate is high enough. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「滑模原理與核心筒的適用條件」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Slipform principle and when cores suit it\" is correct?","options":["滑模適用於所有高層核心筒，只要速度夠快就一定比較省工期。","滑模是一組沿牆體全周連續的模板，由頂部工作平台與軛架連成整體，千斤頂夾住埋在牆中的爬桿往上爬，帶動模板、平台與懸吊的修飾架一起上升。","滑模的速度越快越好，只要千斤頂能力足夠就可以一直加速。"],"optionsEn":["Slipforming suits every high-rise core and is always faster if the rate is high enough.","A slipform is a continuous ring of forms around the whole wall, tied by yokes to a working deck on top.","The faster the slipform the better; it can keep accelerating as long as the jacks are strong enough."],"answer":1,"explanation":"滑模是一組沿牆體全周連續的模板，由頂部工作平台與軛架連成整體，千斤頂夾住埋在牆中的爬桿往上爬，帶動模板、平台與懸吊的修飾架一起上升。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A slipform is a continuous ring of forms around the whole wall, tied by yokes to a working deck on top; jacks grip climbing rods embedded in the wall and climb them, lifting the forms, deck and hanging finishing scaffolds together. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b061-v13-02","title":"滑模原理與核心筒的適用條件：定量估算","titleEn":"Slipform principle and when cores suit it: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「連續滑升工序」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Continuous slipform cycle” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：滑升速度 0.10 m/h、全天 24 h 連續作業時日升 2.4 m；120 m 核心筒需 120/2.4 = 50 天，若計入 10% 的停機與調整時間，約需 50/0.9 ≈ 56 天。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: At 0.10 m/h around the clock the core rises 2.4 m a day; a 120 m core takes 120/2.4 = 50 days, or about 50/0.9 ≈ 56 days allowing 10% for stoppages and adjustments. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在施工規劃階段比較滑模、跳模與自動爬模在工期、人力、混凝土供應與安全上的差異，確認核心筒斷面變化、開口數量、埋件密度與供料能力都支持連續作業；以排程模擬檢查預期停機次數。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: At planning stage compare slipform, jump form and automatic climbing form for programme, labour, concrete supply and safety, and confirm that section changes, the number of openings, embed density and supply capacity all support continuous work; use schedule simulation to check the expected number of stoppages.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"滑升速度 0.10 m/h、全天 24 h 連續作業時日升 2.4 m；120 m 核心筒需 120/2.4 = 50 天，若計入 10% 的停機與調整時間，約需 50/0.9 ≈ 56 天。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"At 0.10 m/h around the clock the core rises 2.4 m a day; a 120 m core takes 120/2.4 = 50 days, or about 50/0.9 ≈ 56 days allowing 10% for stoppages and adjustments. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「滑模原理與核心筒的適用條件」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Slipform principle and when cores suit it\", which statement holds?","options":["滑模速度快，所以埋件位置可以完工後再用鑽孔方式補做。","滑模混凝土是連續澆置的，所以牆內不會有施工縫。","滑升速度 0.10 m/h、全天 24 h 連續作業時日升 2.4 m。"],"optionsEn":["Because slipforming is fast, embed positions can be added afterwards by drilling.","Slipformed walls are cast continuously, so they never contain construction joints.","At 0.10 m/h around the clock the core rises 2.4 m a day."],"answer":2,"explanation":"滑升速度 0.10 m/h、全天 24 h 連續作業時日升 2.4 m；120 m 核心筒需 120/2.4 = 50 天，若計入 10% 的停機與調整時間，約需 50/0.9 ≈ 56 天。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"At 0.10 m/h around the clock the core rises 2.4 m a day; a 120 m core takes 120/2.4 = 50 days, or about 50/0.9 ≈ 56 days allowing 10% for stoppages and adjustments. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b061-v13-03","title":"滑模原理與核心筒的適用條件：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Slipform principle and when cores suit it: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「連續滑升工序」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Continuous slipform cycle” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在施工規劃階段比較滑模、跳模與自動爬模在工期、人力、混凝土供應與安全上的差異，確認核心筒斷面變化、開口數量、埋件密度與供料能力都支持連續作業；以排程模擬檢查預期停機次數。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"At planning stage compare slipform, jump form and automatic climbing form for programme, labour, concrete supply and safety, and confirm that section changes, the number of openings, embed density and supply capacity all support continuous work; use schedule simulation to check the expected number of stoppages. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：決定採用滑模前，要求建築與結構設計把牆厚變化、退縮與開口集中在少數高程，並與滑模專業廠商共同檢討；同時確認預拌廠與運輸能 24 小時供料，且有備援廠。","observationEn":"Site practice: Before choosing slipform, ask the architectural and structural designers to concentrate wall-thickness changes, setbacks and openings at a few levels and review them with the slipform specialist; confirm that the ready-mix plant and haulage can supply 24 hours a day with a back-up plant.","failure":"注意干擾：核心筒斷面每隔幾層就改變牆厚或退縮，滑模被迫頻繁停機改裝，連續作業的優勢消失，反而增加冷縫與品質風險；混凝土供應中斷時，模板內混凝土在靜止中與模板黏結，再啟動時表面被撕裂。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If the core changes wall thickness or steps back every few storeys, the slipform must stop frequently for modification, losing its continuous advantage and adding cold joints and quality risk; if concrete supply is interrupted, concrete in the stationary form bonds to the panels and the surface tears when sliding resumes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在施工規劃階段比較滑模、跳模與自動爬模在工期、人力、混凝土供應與安全上的差異，確認核心筒斷面變化、開口數量、埋件密度與供料能力都支持連續作業；以排程模擬檢查預期停機次數。","textEn":"At planning stage compare slipform, jump form and automatic climbing form for programme, labour, concrete supply and safety, and confirm that section changes, the number of openings, embed density and supply capacity all support continuous work; use schedule simulation to check the expected number of stoppages.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"決定採用滑模前，要求建築與結構設計把牆厚變化、退縮與開口集中在少數高程，並與滑模專業廠商共同檢討；同時確認預拌廠與運輸能 24 小時供料，且有備援廠。","textEn":"Before choosing slipform, ask the architectural and structural designers to concentrate wall-thickness changes, setbacks and openings at a few levels and review them with the slipform specialist; confirm that the ready-mix plant and haulage can supply 24 hours a day with a back-up plant.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「滑模原理與核心筒的適用條件」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Slipform principle and when cores suit it\"?","options":["在施工規劃階段比較滑模、跳模與自動爬模在工期、人力、混凝土供應與安全上的差異，確認核心筒斷面變化、開口數量、埋件密度與供料能力都支持連續作業。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","自動化液壓系統會讓所有千斤頂完全同步，不需要人工量測。"],"optionsEn":["At planning stage compare slipform, jump form and automatic climbing form for programme, labour, concrete supply and safety, and confirm that section changes, the number of openings, embed density and supply capacity all support continuous work.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Automated hydraulics keep every jack perfectly synchronised, so manual levelling is unnecessary."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在施工規劃階段比較滑模、跳模與自動爬模在工期、人力、混凝土供應與安全上的差異，確認核心筒斷面變化、開口數量、埋件密度與供料能力都支持連續作業；以排程模擬檢查預期停機次數。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"At planning stage compare slipform, jump form and automatic climbing form for programme, labour, concrete supply and safety, and confirm that section changes, the number of openings, embed density and supply capacity all support continuous work; use schedule simulation to check the expected number of stoppages. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b061-v13-04","title":"滑模原理與核心筒的適用條件：失效診斷","titleEn":"Slipform principle and when cores suit it: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「連續滑升工序」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Continuous slipform cycle” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"核心筒斷面每隔幾層就改變牆厚或退縮，滑模被迫頻繁停機改裝，連續作業的優勢消失，反而增加冷縫與品質風險；混凝土供應中斷時，模板內混凝土在靜止中與模板黏結，再啟動時表面被撕裂。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If the core changes wall thickness or steps back every few storeys, the slipform must stop frequently for modification, losing its continuous advantage and adding cold joints and quality risk; if concrete supply is interrupted, concrete in the stationary form bonds to the panels and the surface tears when sliding resumes. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：CN Tower 的混凝土塔身就是以液壓爬升千斤頂推動的模具連續成形，並在升高過程中逐步收窄形成錐形。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The CN Tower's concrete shaft was formed this way by a mould driven up by hydraulic climbing jacks, narrowing gradually as it rose to form the taper.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「滑模適用於所有高層核心筒，只要速度夠快就一定比較省工期。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Slipforming suits every high-rise core and is always faster if the rate is high enough.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"核心筒斷面每隔幾層就改變牆厚或退縮，滑模被迫頻繁停機改裝，連續作業的優勢消失，反而增加冷縫與品質風險；混凝土供應中斷時，模板內混凝土在靜止中與模板黏結，再啟動時表面被撕裂。","textEn":"If the core changes wall thickness or steps back every few storeys, the slipform must stop frequently for modification, losing its continuous advantage and adding cold joints and quality risk; if concrete supply is interrupted, concrete in the stationary form bonds to the panels and the surface tears when sliding resumes.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「滑模原理與核心筒的適用條件」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Slipform principle and when cores suit it\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","核心筒斷面每隔幾層就改變牆厚或退縮，滑模被迫頻繁停機改裝，連續作業的優勢消失，反而增加冷縫與品質風險。","滑模的速度越快越好，只要千斤頂能力足夠就可以一直加速。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","If the core changes wall thickness or steps back every few storeys, the slipform must stop frequently for modification, losing its continuous advantage and adding cold joints and quality risk.","The faster the slipform the better; it can keep accelerating as long as the jacks are strong enough."],"answer":1,"explanation":"核心筒斷面每隔幾層就改變牆厚或退縮，滑模被迫頻繁停機改裝，連續作業的優勢消失，反而增加冷縫與品質風險；混凝土供應中斷時，模板內混凝土在靜止中與模板黏結，再啟動時表面被撕裂。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If the core changes wall thickness or steps back every few storeys, the slipform must stop frequently for modification, losing its continuous advantage and adding cold joints and quality risk; if concrete supply is interrupted, concrete in the stationary form bonds to the panels and the surface tears when sliding resumes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b061-v13-05","title":"凝結時間、模板高度與容許滑升速度：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Setting time, form height and allowable slip rate: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「出模混凝土強度」如何影響高層建築核心筒滑模施工的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Concrete strength at form exit” governs force, deformation or durability in “Slipform construction of high-rise cores”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"滑模的核心限制是：混凝土從頂部澆入到從下緣出模的時間，必須長於它達到初凝、可自立的時間。若滑升太快，出模混凝土仍呈塑性，會坍落、鼓出或被模板拖裂；若太慢，混凝土在模板內硬化並與模板黏結，滑升時表面被撕開。凝結時間受水泥種類、緩凝劑、混凝土溫度與氣溫強烈影響，所以滑升速度必須隨日夜溫度調整，而不是固定一個數字。亞特蘭大試驗塔的模板高約 1.2 m（4 ft）。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「出模混凝土強度」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The governing limit of slipforming is that the time from placing at the top to leaving the bottom edge must exceed the time the concrete needs to reach initial set and stand on its own. If sliding is too fast, concrete leaving the form is still plastic and slumps, bulges or is dragged and torn; if too slow, concrete hardens in the form and bonds to it, tearing the surface when sliding resumes. Setting time depends strongly on cement type, retarders, concrete temperature and air temperature, so the slip rate must follow day and night temperatures rather than stay fixed. The forms on the Atlanta test tower were about 1.2 m (4 ft) high. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Concrete strength at form exit” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：容許滑升速度 v_max ≈ h_eff/t_set。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Allowable slip rate v_max ≈ h_eff/t_set.","failure":"常見誤解：「滑模的速度越快越好，只要千斤頂能力足夠就可以一直加速。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The faster the slipform the better; it can keep accelerating as long as the jacks are strong enough.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「出模混凝土強度」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Concrete strength at form exit”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-05-k1","title":"凝結時間、模板高度與容許滑升速度","titleEn":"Setting time, form height and allowable slip rate","text":"滑模的核心限制是：混凝土從頂部澆入到從下緣出模的時間，必須長於它達到初凝、可自立的時間。若滑升太快，出模混凝土仍呈塑性，會坍落、鼓出或被模板拖裂；若太慢，混凝土在模板內硬化並與模板黏結，滑升時表面被撕開。","textEn":"The governing limit of slipforming is that the time from placing at the top to leaving the bottom edge must exceed the time the concrete needs to reach initial set and stand on its own. If sliding is too fast, concrete leaving the form is still plastic and slumps, bulges or is dragged and torn; if too slow, concrete hardens in the form and bonds to it, tearing the surface when sliding resumes.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：滑模的速度越快越好，只要千斤頂能力足夠就可以一直加速。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The faster the slipform the better; it can keep accelerating as long as the jacks are strong enough. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「凝結時間、模板高度與容許滑升速度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Setting time, form height and allowable slip rate\" is correct?","options":["滑模的速度越快越好，只要千斤頂能力足夠就可以一直加速。","千斤頂額定荷重夠大，就代表爬桿與平台一定安全。","滑模的核心限制是：混凝土從頂部澆入到從下緣出模的時間，必須長於它達到初凝、可自立的時間。"],"optionsEn":["The faster the slipform the better; it can keep accelerating as long as the jacks are strong enough.","If the jack rating is high enough, the rods and deck must be safe.","The governing limit of slipforming is that the time from placing at the top to leaving the bottom edge must exceed the time the concrete needs to reach initial set and stand on its own."],"answer":2,"explanation":"滑模的核心限制是：混凝土從頂部澆入到從下緣出模的時間，必須長於它達到初凝、可自立的時間。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The governing limit of slipforming is that the time from placing at the top to leaving the bottom edge must exceed the time the concrete needs to reach initial set and stand on its own. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b061-v13-06","title":"凝結時間、模板高度與容許滑升速度：定量估算","titleEn":"Setting time, form height and allowable slip rate: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「出模混凝土強度」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Concrete strength at form exit” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：容許滑升速度 v_max ≈ h_eff/t_set。模板 1.2 m、頂部預留 0.2 m 時有效高度 h_eff = 1.0 m；20°C 時初凝 4 h，v_max = 1.0/4 = 0.25 m/h；10°C 時凝結時間約加倍為 8 h，v_max 降為 0.125 m/h。實際速度還要留裕度。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Allowable slip rate v_max ≈ h_eff/t_set. With a 1.2 m form and 0.2 m freeboard, h_eff = 1.0 m; at 20°C with initial set at 4 h, v_max = 1.0/4 = 0.25 m/h; at 10°C setting roughly doubles to 8 h and v_max drops to 0.125 m/h. Actual rates keep a margin below these. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：開工前以試拌在不同溫度做凝結時間試驗（貫入阻力法），建立溫度與初凝時間關係；施工中每班以手指按壓或小型貫入計檢查出模面，並記錄混凝土溫度、氣溫與滑升速度，速度調整需由滑模工程師簽記。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before starting, run setting-time tests by penetration resistance on trial batches at several temperatures to relate temperature to initial set; during work check the exit surface each shift by thumb pressure or a small penetrometer, log concrete temperature, air temperature and slip rate, and have the slipform engineer sign every rate change.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"容許滑升速度 v_max ≈ h_eff/t_set。模板 1.2 m、頂部預留 0.2 m 時有效高度 h_eff = 1.0 m；20°C 時初凝 4 h，v_max = 1.0/4 = 0.25 m/h；10°C 時凝結時間約加倍為 8 h，v_max 降為 0.125 m/h。實際速度還要留裕度。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Allowable slip rate v_max ≈ h_eff/t_set. With a 1.2 m form and 0.2 m freeboard, h_eff = 1.0 m; at 20°C with initial set at 4 h, v_max = 1.0/4 = 0.25 m/h; at 10°C setting roughly doubles to 8 h and v_max drops to 0.125 m/h. Actual rates keep a margin below these. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「凝結時間、模板高度與容許滑升速度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Setting time, form height and allowable slip rate\", which statement holds?","options":["容許滑升速度 v_max ≈ h_eff/t_set。","滑模偏了只要在下一段一次調回原位即可。","混凝土在模板內放滿固定小時數就一定可以出模，與溫度無關。"],"optionsEn":["Allowable slip rate v_max ≈ h_eff/t_set.","If the slipform drifts, it can simply be returned to position in the next lift.","Concrete can always leave the form after a fixed number of hours regardless of temperature."],"answer":0,"explanation":"容許滑升速度 v_max ≈ h_eff/t_set。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Allowable slip rate v_max ≈ h_eff/t_set. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b061-v13-07","title":"凝結時間、模板高度與容許滑升速度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Setting time, form height and allowable slip rate: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「出模混凝土強度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Concrete strength at form exit” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"開工前以試拌在不同溫度做凝結時間試驗（貫入阻力法），建立溫度與初凝時間關係；施工中每班以手指按壓或小型貫入計檢查出模面，並記錄混凝土溫度、氣溫與滑升速度，速度調整需由滑模工程師簽記。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before starting, run setting-time tests by penetration resistance on trial batches at several temperatures to relate temperature to initial set; during work check the exit surface each shift by thumb pressure or a small penetrometer, log concrete temperature, air temperature and slip rate, and have the slipform engineer sign every rate change. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：施工計畫應以溫度—速度對照表管理滑升，並規定每班出模面檢查的方法與紀錄；配比中的緩凝劑用量變更須由混凝土供應商與滑模工程師共同同意並先做試驗。","observationEn":"Site practice: Manage slipping with a temperature-versus-rate table in the method statement, specify how the exit surface is checked and recorded each shift, and require joint agreement and prior trials by the concrete supplier and slipform engineer for any change in retarder dosage.","failure":"注意干擾：夜間降溫時仍維持白天速度，出模混凝土未凝結而坍落，牆面出現鼓脹與水平裂縫；白天高溫時速度太慢，混凝土黏住模板，滑升時表面被拉出水平撕裂帶，嚴重時鋼筋外露，需大面積修補。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Keeping the daytime rate as temperatures fall at night lets unset concrete slump out of the form, leaving bulges and horizontal cracks; sliding too slowly in daytime heat lets concrete bond to the form so that each lift drags out horizontal tear bands, in bad cases exposing bars and requiring extensive repair. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"開工前以試拌在不同溫度做凝結時間試驗（貫入阻力法），建立溫度與初凝時間關係；施工中每班以手指按壓或小型貫入計檢查出模面，並記錄混凝土溫度、氣溫與滑升速度，速度調整需由滑模工程師簽記。","textEn":"Before starting, run setting-time tests by penetration resistance on trial batches at several temperatures to relate temperature to initial set; during work check the exit surface each shift by thumb pressure or a small penetrometer, log concrete temperature, air temperature and slip rate, and have the slipform engineer sign every rate change.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"施工計畫應以溫度—速度對照表管理滑升，並規定每班出模面檢查的方法與紀錄；配比中的緩凝劑用量變更須由混凝土供應商與滑模工程師共同同意並先做試驗。","textEn":"Manage slipping with a temperature-versus-rate table in the method statement, specify how the exit surface is checked and recorded each shift, and require joint agreement and prior trials by the concrete supplier and slipform engineer for any change in retarder dosage.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「凝結時間、模板高度與容許滑升速度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Setting time, form height and allowable slip rate\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","開工前以試拌在不同溫度做凝結時間試驗（貫入阻力法），建立溫度與初凝時間關係。","核心筒以後會被裝修包覆，所以滑模牆面的養護不重要。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Before starting, run setting-time tests by penetration resistance on trial batches at several temperatures to relate temperature to initial set.","Core walls will be covered by finishes later, so curing slipformed surfaces does not matter."],"answer":1,"explanation":"開工前以試拌在不同溫度做凝結時間試驗（貫入阻力法），建立溫度與初凝時間關係；施工中每班以手指按壓或小型貫入計檢查出模面，並記錄混凝土溫度、氣溫與滑升速度，速度調整需由滑模工程師簽記。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before starting, run setting-time tests by penetration resistance on trial batches at several temperatures to relate temperature to initial set; during work check the exit surface each shift by thumb pressure or a small penetrometer, log concrete temperature, air temperature and slip rate, and have the slipform engineer sign every rate change. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b061-v13-08","title":"凝結時間、模板高度與容許滑升速度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Setting time, form height and allowable slip rate: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「出模混凝土強度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Concrete strength at form exit” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"夜間降溫時仍維持白天速度，出模混凝土未凝結而坍落，牆面出現鼓脹與水平裂縫；白天高溫時速度太慢，混凝土黏住模板，滑升時表面被拉出水平撕裂帶，嚴重時鋼筋外露，需大面積修補。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Keeping the daytime rate as temperatures fall at night lets unset concrete slump out of the form, leaving bulges and horizontal cracks; sliding too slowly in daytime heat lets concrete bond to the form so that each lift drags out horizontal tear bands, in bad cases exposing bars and requiring extensive repair. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：亞特蘭大試驗塔的模板高約 1.2 m（4 ft）。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The forms on the Atlanta test tower were about 1.2 m (4 ft) high.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「滑模的速度越快越好，只要千斤頂能力足夠就可以一直加速。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The faster the slipform the better; it can keep accelerating as long as the jacks are strong enough.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"夜間降溫時仍維持白天速度，出模混凝土未凝結而坍落，牆面出現鼓脹與水平裂縫；白天高溫時速度太慢，混凝土黏住模板，滑升時表面被拉出水平撕裂帶，嚴重時鋼筋外露，需大面積修補。","textEn":"Keeping the daytime rate as temperatures fall at night lets unset concrete slump out of the form, leaving bulges and horizontal cracks; sliding too slowly in daytime heat lets concrete bond to the form so that each lift drags out horizontal tear bands, in bad cases exposing bars and requiring extensive repair.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「凝結時間、模板高度與容許滑升速度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Setting time, form height and allowable slip rate\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","千斤頂額定荷重夠大，就代表爬桿與平台一定安全。","夜間降溫時仍維持白天速度，出模混凝土未凝結而坍落，牆面出現鼓脹與水平裂縫。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","If the jack rating is high enough, the rods and deck must be safe.","Keeping the daytime rate as temperatures fall at night lets unset concrete slump out of the form, leaving bulges and horizontal cracks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"夜間降溫時仍維持白天速度，出模混凝土未凝結而坍落，牆面出現鼓脹與水平裂縫；白天高溫時速度太慢，混凝土黏住模板，滑升時表面被拉出水平撕裂帶，嚴重時鋼筋外露，需大面積修補。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Keeping the daytime rate as temperatures fall at night lets unset concrete slump out of the form, leaving bulges and horizontal cracks; sliding too slowly in daytime heat lets concrete bond to the form so that each lift drags out horizontal tear bands, in bad cases exposing bars and requiring extensive repair. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b061-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「爬桿、千斤頂與平台荷重」與「鋼筋、埋件與開口的連續協調」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Climbing rods, jacks and deck loads\" and \"Continuous coordination of rebar, embeds and openings\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b061-v13-09","title":"爬桿、千斤頂與平台荷重：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Climbing rods, jacks and deck loads: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「千斤頂與爬桿」如何影響高層建築核心筒滑模施工的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Jacks and climbing rods” governs force, deformation or durability in “Slipform construction of high-rise cores”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"滑模的全部重量，包括模板、軛架、工作平台、懸吊修飾架、堆放材料、人員以及模板與混凝土之間的摩擦力，都由數十到上百支千斤頂經爬桿傳入已硬化的牆體。爬桿在剛硬化的混凝土與千斤頂之間有一段未受側向支撐的長度，容易挫屈；因此實際能用的單支荷重常由爬桿挫屈而非千斤頂額定值控制。美國 OSHA 1926.703 規定爬桿須為專用設計且在未埋入混凝土處要適當支撐，千斤頂荷重不得超過額定能力，並須有斷電時自動鎖住的機械裝置。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「千斤頂與爬桿」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The entire weight of the slipform, including forms, yokes, deck, hanging finishing scaffolds, stored materials, people and the friction between forms and concrete, passes through dozens or over a hundred jacks and their climbing rods into the hardened wall. Between the newly hardened concrete and the jack each rod has an unbraced length that is prone to buckling, so the usable load per rod is often governed by rod buckling rather than the jack rating. US OSHA 1926.703 requires climbing rods to be specifically designed and braced where not encased in concrete, jack loads to stay within rated capacity, and automatic holding devices to hold the forms if power fails. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Jacks and climbing rods” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：爬桿 48.3×4 mm 鋼管，I ≈ 137,700 mm⁴、無支撐長 1.5 m，P_cr = π²EI/L² = π²×200,000×137,700/1,500² ≈ 121 kN，取安全係數 2.5 得 48 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A 48.3×4 mm tube rod has I ≈ 137,700 mm⁴; with 1.5 m unbraced, P_cr = π²EI/L² = π²×200,000×137,700/1,500² ≈ 121 kN, or 48 kN with a factor of 2.5.","failure":"常見誤解：「千斤頂額定荷重夠大，就代表爬桿與平台一定安全。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the jack rating is high enough, the rods and deck must be safe.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「千斤頂與爬桿」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Jacks and climbing rods”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-09-k1","title":"爬桿、千斤頂與平台荷重","titleEn":"Climbing rods, jacks and deck loads","text":"滑模的全部重量，包括模板、軛架、工作平台、懸吊修飾架、堆放材料、人員以及模板與混凝土之間的摩擦力，都由數十到上百支千斤頂經爬桿傳入已硬化的牆體。爬桿在剛硬化的混凝土與千斤頂之間有一段未受側向支撐的長度，容易挫屈；因此實際能用的單支荷重常由爬桿挫屈而非千斤頂額定值控制。","textEn":"The entire weight of the slipform, including forms, yokes, deck, hanging finishing scaffolds, stored materials, people and the friction between forms and concrete, passes through dozens or over a hundred jacks and their climbing rods into the hardened wall. Between the newly hardened concrete and the jack each rod has an unbraced length that is prone to buckling, so the usable load per rod is often governed by rod buckling rather than the jack rating.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：千斤頂額定荷重夠大，就代表爬桿與平台一定安全。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the jack rating is high enough, the rods and deck must be safe. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「爬桿、千斤頂與平台荷重」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Climbing rods, jacks and deck loads\" is correct?","options":["滑模的全部重量，包括模板、軛架、工作平台、懸吊修飾架、堆放材料、人員以及模板與混凝土之間的摩擦力，都由數十到上百支千斤頂經爬桿傳入已硬化的牆體。","千斤頂額定荷重夠大，就代表爬桿與平台一定安全。","滑模速度快，所以埋件位置可以完工後再用鑽孔方式補做。"],"optionsEn":["The entire weight of the slipform, including forms, yokes, deck, hanging finishing scaffolds, stored materials, people and the friction between forms and concrete, passes through dozens or over a hundred jacks and their climbing rods into the hardened wall.","If the jack rating is high enough, the rods and deck must be safe.","Because slipforming is fast, embed positions can be added afterwards by drilling."],"answer":0,"explanation":"滑模的全部重量，包括模板、軛架、工作平台、懸吊修飾架、堆放材料、人員以及模板與混凝土之間的摩擦力，都由數十到上百支千斤頂經爬桿傳入已硬化的牆體。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The entire weight of the slipform, including forms, yokes, deck, hanging finishing scaffolds, stored materials, people and the friction between forms and concrete, passes through dozens or over a hundred jacks and their climbing rods into the hardened wall. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b061-v13-10","title":"爬桿、千斤頂與平台荷重：定量估算","titleEn":"Climbing rods, jacks and deck loads: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「千斤頂與爬桿」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Jacks and climbing rods” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：爬桿 48.3×4 mm 鋼管，I ≈ 137,700 mm⁴、無支撐長 1.5 m，P_cr = π²EI/L² = π²×200,000×137,700/1,500² ≈ 121 kN，取安全係數 2.5 得 48 kN。平台荷重：靜載 250 t、活載 90 t、模板摩擦 2 kPa×(150 m×2 面×1.2 m) = 720 kN，合計 ≈ 4,055 kN，需約 4,055/48 ≈ 84 支千斤頂。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A 48.3×4 mm tube rod has I ≈ 137,700 mm⁴; with 1.5 m unbraced, P_cr = π²EI/L² = π²×200,000×137,700/1,500² ≈ 121 kN, or 48 kN with a factor of 2.5. Deck loads: 250 t dead, 90 t live and form friction 2 kPa×(150 m×2 faces×1.2 m) = 720 kN, total about 4,055 kN, needing about 4,055/48 ≈ 84 jacks. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：滑模設計計算書須列出每支千斤頂的分擔荷重、爬桿挫屈長度與安全係數，並由滑模設計者簽認；現場在開滑前檢查每支千斤頂油壓、行程與自動鎖定功能，滑升中巡查爬桿是否彎曲，平台堆料以標示的容許荷重管控。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: The slipform design calculations must list each jack's share of load, rod buckling length and safety factor, signed by the slipform designer; before starting check each jack's pressure, stroke and automatic holding function, inspect rods for bending during sliding, and control deck stockpiles against posted load limits.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"爬桿 48.3×4 mm 鋼管，I ≈ 137,700 mm⁴、無支撐長 1.5 m，P_cr = π²EI/L² = π²×200,000×137,700/1,500² ≈ 121 kN，取安全係數 2.5 得 48 kN。平台荷重：靜載 250 t、活載 90 t、模板摩擦 2 kPa×(150 m×2 面×1.2 m) = 720 kN，合計 ≈ 4,055 kN，需約 4,055/48 ≈ 84 支千斤頂。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"A 48.3×4 mm tube rod has I ≈ 137,700 mm⁴; with 1.5 m unbraced, P_cr = π²EI/L² = π²×200,000×137,700/1,500² ≈ 121 kN, or 48 kN with a factor of 2.5. Deck loads: 250 t dead, 90 t live and form friction 2 kPa×(150 m×2 faces×1.2 m) = 720 kN, total about 4,055 kN, needing about 4,055/48 ≈ 84 jacks. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「爬桿、千斤頂與平台荷重」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Climbing rods, jacks and deck loads\", which statement holds?","options":["滑模混凝土是連續澆置的，所以牆內不會有施工縫。","爬桿 48.3×4 mm 鋼管，I ≈ 137,700 mm⁴、無支撐長 1.5 m，P_cr = π²EI/L² = π²×200,000×137,700/1,500² ≈ 121 kN，取安全係數 2.5 得 48 kN。","自動化液壓系統會讓所有千斤頂完全同步，不需要人工量測。"],"optionsEn":["Slipformed walls are cast continuously, so they never contain construction joints.","A 48.3×4 mm tube rod has I ≈ 137,700 mm⁴; with 1.5 m unbraced, P_cr = π²EI/L² = π²×200,000×137,700/1,500² ≈ 121 kN, or 48 kN with a factor of 2.5.","Automated hydraulics keep every jack perfectly synchronised, so manual levelling is unnecessary."],"answer":1,"explanation":"爬桿 48.3×4 mm 鋼管，I ≈ 137,700 mm⁴、無支撐長 1.5 m，P_cr = π²EI/L² = π²×200,000×137,700/1,500² ≈ 121 kN，取安全係數 2.5 得 48 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A 48.3×4 mm tube rod has I ≈ 137,700 mm⁴; with 1.5 m unbraced, P_cr = π²EI/L² = π²×200,000×137,700/1,500² ≈ 121 kN, or 48 kN with a factor of 2.5. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b061-v13-11","title":"爬桿、千斤頂與平台荷重：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Climbing rods, jacks and deck loads: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「千斤頂與爬桿」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Jacks and climbing rods” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"滑模設計計算書須列出每支千斤頂的分擔荷重、爬桿挫屈長度與安全係數，並由滑模設計者簽認；現場在開滑前檢查每支千斤頂油壓、行程與自動鎖定功能，滑升中巡查爬桿是否彎曲，平台堆料以標示的容許荷重管控。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"The slipform design calculations must list each jack's share of load, rod buckling length and safety factor, signed by the slipform designer; before starting check each jack's pressure, stroke and automatic holding function, inspect rods for bending during sliding, and control deck stockpiles against posted load limits. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：平台上應以油漆或標牌劃出堆料區與容許荷重，吊料前由平台負責人確認；千斤頂與爬桿屬臨時工程關鍵構件，開滑前設停檢點由臨時工程設計者與施工主管共同簽認。","observationEn":"Site practice: Mark stockpile zones and allowable loads on the deck with paint or signs and have the deck supervisor approve each delivery; jacks and rods are critical temporary-works components, so set a pre-start hold point signed by the temporary-works designer and the construction manager.","failure":"注意干擾：平台上集中堆放鋼筋，使局部千斤頂超載，爬桿在未支撐段彎曲，平台傾斜並把模板扭曲；斷電或油管破裂時若千斤頂沒有自動鎖定，整個平台可能下滑，造成人員墜落。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Concentrating rebar bundles on the deck overloads local jacks, rods bend in their unbraced length, the deck tilts and the forms are twisted; if power fails or a hose bursts and the jacks lack automatic holding, the whole deck may slide down and throw workers off. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"滑模設計計算書須列出每支千斤頂的分擔荷重、爬桿挫屈長度與安全係數，並由滑模設計者簽認；現場在開滑前檢查每支千斤頂油壓、行程與自動鎖定功能，滑升中巡查爬桿是否彎曲，平台堆料以標示的容許荷重管控。","textEn":"The slipform design calculations must list each jack's share of load, rod buckling length and safety factor, signed by the slipform designer; before starting check each jack's pressure, stroke and automatic holding function, inspect rods for bending during sliding, and control deck stockpiles against posted load limits.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"平台上應以油漆或標牌劃出堆料區與容許荷重，吊料前由平台負責人確認；千斤頂與爬桿屬臨時工程關鍵構件，開滑前設停檢點由臨時工程設計者與施工主管共同簽認。","textEn":"Mark stockpile zones and allowable loads on the deck with paint or signs and have the deck supervisor approve each delivery; jacks and rods are critical temporary-works components, so set a pre-start hold point signed by the temporary-works designer and the construction manager.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「爬桿、千斤頂與平台荷重」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Climbing rods, jacks and deck loads\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","核心筒驗收只要總高度與整體垂直度合格就足夠。","滑模設計計算書須列出每支千斤頂的分擔荷重、爬桿挫屈長度與安全係數，並由滑模設計者簽認。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A core passes acceptance if its total height and overall verticality are within tolerance.","The slipform design calculations must list each jack's share of load, rod buckling length and safety factor, signed by the slipform designer."],"answer":2,"explanation":"滑模設計計算書須列出每支千斤頂的分擔荷重、爬桿挫屈長度與安全係數，並由滑模設計者簽認；現場在開滑前檢查每支千斤頂油壓、行程與自動鎖定功能，滑升中巡查爬桿是否彎曲，平台堆料以標示的容許荷重管控。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"The slipform design calculations must list each jack's share of load, rod buckling length and safety factor, signed by the slipform designer; before starting check each jack's pressure, stroke and automatic holding function, inspect rods for bending during sliding, and control deck stockpiles against posted load limits. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b061-v13-12","title":"爬桿、千斤頂與平台荷重：失效診斷","titleEn":"Climbing rods, jacks and deck loads: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「千斤頂與爬桿」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Jacks and climbing rods” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"平台上集中堆放鋼筋，使局部千斤頂超載，爬桿在未支撐段彎曲，平台傾斜並把模板扭曲；斷電或油管破裂時若千斤頂沒有自動鎖定，整個平台可能下滑，造成人員墜落。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Concentrating rebar bundles on the deck overloads local jacks, rods bend in their unbraced length, the deck tilts and the forms are twisted; if power fails or a hose bursts and the jacks lack automatic holding, the whole deck may slide down and throw workers off. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：美國 OSHA 1926.703 規定爬桿須為專用設計且在未埋入混凝土處要適當支撐，千斤頂荷重不得超過額定能力，並須有斷電時自動鎖住的機械裝置。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: US OSHA 1926.703 requires climbing rods to be specifically designed and braced where not encased in concrete, jack loads to stay within rated capacity, and automatic holding devices to hold the forms if power fails.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「千斤頂額定荷重夠大，就代表爬桿與平台一定安全。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the jack rating is high enough, the rods and deck must be safe.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"平台上集中堆放鋼筋，使局部千斤頂超載，爬桿在未支撐段彎曲，平台傾斜並把模板扭曲；斷電或油管破裂時若千斤頂沒有自動鎖定，整個平台可能下滑，造成人員墜落。","textEn":"Concentrating rebar bundles on the deck overloads local jacks, rods bend in their unbraced length, the deck tilts and the forms are twisted; if power fails or a hose bursts and the jacks lack automatic holding, the whole deck may slide down and throw workers off.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「爬桿、千斤頂與平台荷重」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Climbing rods, jacks and deck loads\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["平台上集中堆放鋼筋，使局部千斤頂超載，爬桿在未支撐段彎曲，平台傾斜並把模板扭曲；斷電或油管破裂時若千斤頂沒有自動鎖定，整個平台可能下滑，造成人員墜落。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","滑模速度快，所以埋件位置可以完工後再用鑽孔方式補做。"],"optionsEn":["Concentrating rebar bundles on the deck overloads local jacks, rods bend in their unbraced length, the deck tilts and the forms are twisted.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Because slipforming is fast, embed positions can be added afterwards by drilling."],"answer":0,"explanation":"平台上集中堆放鋼筋，使局部千斤頂超載，爬桿在未支撐段彎曲，平台傾斜並把模板扭曲；斷電或油管破裂時若千斤頂沒有自動鎖定，整個平台可能下滑，造成人員墜落。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Concentrating rebar bundles on the deck overloads local jacks, rods bend in their unbraced length, the deck tilts and the forms are twisted; if power fails or a hose bursts and the jacks lack automatic holding, the whole deck may slide down and throw workers off. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b061-v13-13","title":"鋼筋、埋件與開口的連續協調：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Continuous coordination of rebar, embeds and openings: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「埋件與開口」如何影響高層建築核心筒滑模施工的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Embeds and openings” governs force, deformation or durability in “Slipform construction of high-rise cores”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"滑模不會停下來等人，所以鋼筋、門窗開口框、樓板連接用的預埋鋼板、續接器與機電套管，都必須在模板經過之前到位。亞特蘭大試驗塔的核心筒有近 190 個開口、超過 3,300 塊預埋鋼板，單一高程最多約 200 件；這使埋件定位成為滑模最主要的品質風險。樓板通常在核心筒完成後再施作，因此牆內必須預留續接器或剪力鍵與樓板相接，任何漏埋都只能事後鑽孔植筋。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「埋件與開口」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A slipform never stops to wait, so rebar, door and window boxouts, embed plates for floor connections, couplers and services sleeves must all be in place before the form passes. The Atlanta test tower's core had nearly 190 openings and over 3,300 embed plates, with up to about 200 pieces at a single elevation, which made embed placement the main quality risk of the slipform. Floors are usually built after the core, so the walls must contain couplers or shear keys to receive them, and any missed item can only be fixed later by drilling and bonding. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Embeds and openings” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：埋件 3,300 件、滑升約 54 天，平均每天 3,300/54 ≈ 61 件，相當於每小時約 2.5 件。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: 3,300 embeds over about 54 days of sliding average 3,300/54 ≈ 61 per day, about 2.5 per hour.","failure":"常見誤解：「滑模速度快，所以埋件位置可以完工後再用鑽孔方式補做。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Because slipforming is fast, embed positions can be added afterwards by drilling.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「埋件與開口」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Embeds and openings”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-13-k1","title":"鋼筋、埋件與開口的連續協調","titleEn":"Continuous coordination of rebar, embeds and openings","text":"滑模不會停下來等人，所以鋼筋、門窗開口框、樓板連接用的預埋鋼板、續接器與機電套管，都必須在模板經過之前到位。亞特蘭大試驗塔的核心筒有近 190 個開口、超過 3,300 塊預埋鋼板，單一高程最多約 200 件；這使埋件定位成為滑模最主要的品質風險。","textEn":"A slipform never stops to wait, so rebar, door and window boxouts, embed plates for floor connections, couplers and services sleeves must all be in place before the form passes. The Atlanta test tower's core had nearly 190 openings and over 3,300 embed plates, with up to about 200 pieces at a single elevation, which made embed placement the main quality risk of the slipform.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：滑模速度快，所以埋件位置可以完工後再用鑽孔方式補做。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Because slipforming is fast, embed positions can be added afterwards by drilling. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鋼筋、埋件與開口的連續協調」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Continuous coordination of rebar, embeds and openings\" is correct?","options":["滑模速度快，所以埋件位置可以完工後再用鑽孔方式補做。","滑模不會停下來等人，所以鋼筋、門窗開口框、樓板連接用的預埋鋼板、續接器與機電套管，都必須在模板經過之前到位。","滑模偏了只要在下一段一次調回原位即可。"],"optionsEn":["Because slipforming is fast, embed positions can be added afterwards by drilling.","A slipform never stops to wait, so rebar, door and window boxouts, embed plates for floor connections, couplers and services sleeves must all be in place before the form passes.","If the slipform drifts, it can simply be returned to position in the next lift."],"answer":1,"explanation":"滑模不會停下來等人，所以鋼筋、門窗開口框、樓板連接用的預埋鋼板、續接器與機電套管，都必須在模板經過之前到位。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A slipform never stops to wait, so rebar, door and window boxouts, embed plates for floor connections, couplers and services sleeves must all be in place before the form passes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b061-v13-14","title":"鋼筋、埋件與開口的連續協調：定量估算","titleEn":"Continuous coordination of rebar, embeds and openings: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「埋件與開口」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Embeds and openings” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：埋件 3,300 件、滑升約 54 天，平均每天 3,300/54 ≈ 61 件，相當於每小時約 2.5 件。水平筋：牆長 150 m、雙面、間距 200 mm，每米高 5 層×2 面×150 m = 1,500 m，φ16 每米 1.58 kg，約 2,370 kg/m；日升 2.29 m 時每天約 5.4 t 水平筋。數值中的埋件數與天數取自公開報導，其餘為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: 3,300 embeds over about 54 days of sliding average 3,300/54 ≈ 61 per day, about 2.5 per hour. Horizontal bars: 150 m of wall, two faces at 200 mm spacing give 5 layers×2 faces×150 m = 1,500 m per metre of height, at 1.58 kg/m for φ16 about 2,370 kg/m, or about 5.4 t per day at 2.29 m per day. Embed count and days come from public reporting; the rest are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以三維模型產生按高程排序的埋件與開口清單，每件有編號、座標與照片欄；平台上設專人在模板通過前逐件勾核位置與固定，並由測量人員以全站儀抽測關鍵埋件，紀錄與滑升日誌同步。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Generate an elevation-sorted list of embeds and openings from the 3D model, each with a number, coordinates and a photo field; assign a person on the deck to tick off position and fixing of each item before the form passes, have surveyors check key embeds with a total station, and keep the records in step with the slip log.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"埋件 3,300 件、滑升約 54 天，平均每天 3,300/54 ≈ 61 件，相當於每小時約 2.5 件。水平筋：牆長 150 m、雙面、間距 200 mm，每米高 5 層×2 面×150 m = 1,500 m，φ16 每米 1.58 kg，約 2,370 kg/m；日升 2.29 m 時每天約 5.4 t 水平筋。數值中的埋件數與天數取自公開報導，其餘為教學假設。","textEn":"3,300 embeds over about 54 days of sliding average 3,300/54 ≈ 61 per day, about 2.5 per hour. Horizontal bars: 150 m of wall, two faces at 200 mm spacing give 5 layers×2 faces×150 m = 1,500 m per metre of height, at 1.58 kg/m for φ16 about 2,370 kg/m, or about 5.4 t per day at 2.29 m per day. Embed count and days come from public reporting; the rest are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鋼筋、埋件與開口的連續協調」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Continuous coordination of rebar, embeds and openings\", which statement holds?","options":["混凝土在模板內放滿固定小時數就一定可以出模，與溫度無關。","核心筒以後會被裝修包覆，所以滑模牆面的養護不重要。","埋件 3,300 件、滑升約 54 天，平均每天 3,300/54 ≈ 61 件，相當於每小時約 2.5 件。"],"optionsEn":["Concrete can always leave the form after a fixed number of hours regardless of temperature.","Core walls will be covered by finishes later, so curing slipformed surfaces does not matter.","3,300 embeds over about 54 days of sliding average 3,300/54 ≈ 61 per day, about 2.5 per hour."],"answer":2,"explanation":"埋件 3,300 件、滑升約 54 天，平均每天 3,300/54 ≈ 61 件，相當於每小時約 2.5 件。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"3,300 embeds over about 54 days of sliding average 3,300/54 ≈ 61 per day, about 2.5 per hour. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b061-v13-15","title":"鋼筋、埋件與開口的連續協調：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Continuous coordination of rebar, embeds and openings: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「埋件與開口」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Embeds and openings” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以三維模型產生按高程排序的埋件與開口清單，每件有編號、座標與照片欄；平台上設專人在模板通過前逐件勾核位置與固定，並由測量人員以全站儀抽測關鍵埋件，紀錄與滑升日誌同步。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Generate an elevation-sorted list of embeds and openings from the 3D model, each with a number, coordinates and a photo field; assign a person on the deck to tick off position and fixing of each item before the form passes, have surveyors check key embeds with a total station, and keep the records in step with the slip log. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：開滑前凍結埋件與開口設計，之後的變更要經過專門的變更程序並在平台上公告；每一高程的埋件勾核表需由平台品管人員與監造簽名，未簽不得繼續滑升超過該高程。","observationEn":"Site practice: Freeze the embed and opening design before sliding starts, route later changes through a dedicated change procedure posted on the deck, and require the deck quality controller and the resident engineer to sign each elevation's checklist before sliding continues past it.","failure":"注意干擾：埋件高程錯誤或漏埋，樓板鋼梁無法連接，只能事後鑽孔植入錨栓，承載力與耐久都打折；開口框固定不牢在滑升中被拖動，門洞位置偏移，電梯門框無法安裝。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Embeds at the wrong level or missing leave floor beams with nothing to connect to, forcing post-drilled anchors with reduced capacity and durability; poorly fixed boxouts dragged by the moving form shift door openings so that elevator door frames cannot be installed. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以三維模型產生按高程排序的埋件與開口清單，每件有編號、座標與照片欄；平台上設專人在模板通過前逐件勾核位置與固定，並由測量人員以全站儀抽測關鍵埋件，紀錄與滑升日誌同步。","textEn":"Generate an elevation-sorted list of embeds and openings from the 3D model, each with a number, coordinates and a photo field; assign a person on the deck to tick off position and fixing of each item before the form passes, have surveyors check key embeds with a total station, and keep the records in step with the slip log.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"開滑前凍結埋件與開口設計，之後的變更要經過專門的變更程序並在平台上公告；每一高程的埋件勾核表需由平台品管人員與監造簽名，未簽不得繼續滑升超過該高程。","textEn":"Freeze the embed and opening design before sliding starts, route later changes through a dedicated change procedure posted on the deck, and require the deck quality controller and the resident engineer to sign each elevation's checklist before sliding continues past it.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鋼筋、埋件與開口的連續協調」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Continuous coordination of rebar, embeds and openings\"?","options":["以三維模型產生按高程排序的埋件與開口清單，每件有編號、座標與照片欄。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","滑模適用於所有高層核心筒，只要速度夠快就一定比較省工期。"],"optionsEn":["Generate an elevation-sorted list of embeds and openings from the 3D model, each with a number, coordinates and a photo field.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Slipforming suits every high-rise core and is always faster if the rate is high enough."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以三維模型產生按高程排序的埋件與開口清單，每件有編號、座標與照片欄；平台上設專人在模板通過前逐件勾核位置與固定，並由測量人員以全站儀抽測關鍵埋件，紀錄與滑升日誌同步。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Generate an elevation-sorted list of embeds and openings from the 3D model, each with a number, coordinates and a photo field; assign a person on the deck to tick off position and fixing of each item before the form passes, have surveyors check key embeds with a total station, and keep the records in step with the slip log. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b061-v13-16","title":"鋼筋、埋件與開口的連續協調：失效診斷","titleEn":"Continuous coordination of rebar, embeds and openings: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「埋件與開口」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Embeds and openings” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"埋件高程錯誤或漏埋，樓板鋼梁無法連接，只能事後鑽孔植入錨栓，承載力與耐久都打折；開口框固定不牢在滑升中被拖動，門洞位置偏移，電梯門框無法安裝。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Embeds at the wrong level or missing leave floor beams with nothing to connect to, forcing post-drilled anchors with reduced capacity and durability; poorly fixed boxouts dragged by the moving form shift door openings so that elevator door frames cannot be installed. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：樓板通常在核心筒完成後再施作，因此牆內必須預留續接器或剪力鍵與樓板相接，任何漏埋都只能事後鑽孔植筋。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Floors are usually built after the core, so the walls must contain couplers or shear keys to receive them, and any missed item can only be fixed later by drilling and bonding.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「滑模速度快，所以埋件位置可以完工後再用鑽孔方式補做。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Because slipforming is fast, embed positions can be added afterwards by drilling.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"埋件高程錯誤或漏埋，樓板鋼梁無法連接，只能事後鑽孔植入錨栓，承載力與耐久都打折；開口框固定不牢在滑升中被拖動，門洞位置偏移，電梯門框無法安裝。","textEn":"Embeds at the wrong level or missing leave floor beams with nothing to connect to, forcing post-drilled anchors with reduced capacity and durability; poorly fixed boxouts dragged by the moving form shift door openings so that elevator door frames cannot be installed.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鋼筋、埋件與開口的連續協調」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Continuous coordination of rebar, embeds and openings\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","埋件高程錯誤或漏埋，樓板鋼梁無法連接，只能事後鑽孔植入錨栓，承載力與耐久都打折；開口框固定不牢在滑升中被拖動，門洞位置偏移，電梯門框無法安裝。","滑模偏了只要在下一段一次調回原位即可。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Embeds at the wrong level or missing leave floor beams with nothing to connect to, forcing post-drilled anchors with reduced capacity and durability.","If the slipform drifts, it can simply be returned to position in the next lift."],"answer":1,"explanation":"埋件高程錯誤或漏埋，樓板鋼梁無法連接，只能事後鑽孔植入錨栓，承載力與耐久都打折；開口框固定不牢在滑升中被拖動，門洞位置偏移，電梯門框無法安裝。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Embeds at the wrong level or missing leave floor beams with nothing to connect to, forcing post-drilled anchors with reduced capacity and durability; poorly fixed boxouts dragged by the moving form shift door openings so that elevator door frames cannot be installed. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b061-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「垂直度、扭轉與平台水平的修正」與「計畫停機、冷縫處理與惡劣天候」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Correcting verticality, twist and deck level\" and \"Planned stops, cold joints and bad weather\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b061-v13-17","title":"垂直度、扭轉與平台水平的修正：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Correcting verticality, twist and deck level: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「垂直度與扭轉控制」如何影響高層建築核心筒滑模施工的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Verticality and twist control” governs force, deformation or durability in “Slipform construction of high-rise cores”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"滑模的幾何誤差會沿高度累積：平台只要稍微傾斜，模板就會往低側漂移；千斤頂行程不一致會讓平台扭轉，核心筒隨之旋轉。修正不能一次大幅調整，因為模板內的混凝土尚未硬化，突然改變方向會在牆面留下錯台或裂縫，只能以小坡度在數公尺高度內逐漸拉回。CN Tower 塔身邊升邊收窄，更需要精確控制幾何。亞特蘭大試驗塔的牆面垂直偏差控制在約 ±6 mm（±¼ in）以內。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「垂直度與扭轉控制」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Slipform geometry errors accumulate with height: a slightly tilted deck makes the forms drift toward the low side, and uneven jack strokes twist the deck so the core rotates. Corrections cannot be large and sudden, because the concrete in the form has not hardened and an abrupt change leaves steps or cracks; drift must be pulled back gradually over several metres at a small gradient. The CN Tower shaft narrowed as it rose, demanding even tighter geometric control. At the Atlanta test tower the vertical surface deviation was held within about ±6 mm (±¼ in). Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Verticality and twist control” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：若量到核心筒偏離 20 mm，以 1:500 的修正坡度拉回，需要的修正高度 = 20 mm×500 = 10 m；日升 2.29 m 時約需 10/2.29 ≈ 4.4 天才能完全修正，所以偏差必須在小時就被發現。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: If the core is found 20 mm off line and corrected at a gradient of 1:500, the correction height is 20 mm×500 = 10 m; at 2.29 m per day that takes about 10/2.29 ≈ 4.4 days, so deviations must be caught while still small.","failure":"常見誤解：「滑模偏了只要在下一段一次調回原位即可。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"If the slipform drifts, it can simply be returned to position in the next lift.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「垂直度與扭轉控制」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Verticality and twist control”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-17-k1","title":"垂直度、扭轉與平台水平的修正","titleEn":"Correcting verticality, twist and deck level","text":"滑模的幾何誤差會沿高度累積：平台只要稍微傾斜，模板就會往低側漂移；千斤頂行程不一致會讓平台扭轉，核心筒隨之旋轉。修正不能一次大幅調整，因為模板內的混凝土尚未硬化，突然改變方向會在牆面留下錯台或裂縫，只能以小坡度在數公尺高度內逐漸拉回。","textEn":"Slipform geometry errors accumulate with height: a slightly tilted deck makes the forms drift toward the low side, and uneven jack strokes twist the deck so the core rotates. Corrections cannot be large and sudden, because the concrete in the form has not hardened and an abrupt change leaves steps or cracks; drift must be pulled back gradually over several metres at a small gradient.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：滑模偏了只要在下一段一次調回原位即可。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: If the slipform drifts, it can simply be returned to position in the next lift. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「垂直度、扭轉與平台水平的修正」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Correcting verticality, twist and deck level\" is correct?","options":["滑模偏了只要在下一段一次調回原位即可。","滑模混凝土是連續澆置的，所以牆內不會有施工縫。","滑模的幾何誤差會沿高度累積：平台只要稍微傾斜，模板就會往低側漂移；千斤頂行程不一致會讓平台扭轉，核心筒隨之旋轉。"],"optionsEn":["If the slipform drifts, it can simply be returned to position in the next lift.","Slipformed walls are cast continuously, so they never contain construction joints.","Slipform geometry errors accumulate with height: a slightly tilted deck makes the forms drift toward the low side, and uneven jack strokes twist the deck so the core rotates."],"answer":2,"explanation":"滑模的幾何誤差會沿高度累積：平台只要稍微傾斜，模板就會往低側漂移；千斤頂行程不一致會讓平台扭轉，核心筒隨之旋轉。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Slipform geometry errors accumulate with height: a slightly tilted deck makes the forms drift toward the low side, and uneven jack strokes twist the deck so the core rotates. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b061-v13-18","title":"垂直度、扭轉與平台水平的修正：定量估算","titleEn":"Correcting verticality, twist and deck level: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「垂直度與扭轉控制」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Verticality and twist control” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：若量到核心筒偏離 20 mm，以 1:500 的修正坡度拉回，需要的修正高度 = 20 mm×500 = 10 m；日升 2.29 m 時約需 10/2.29 ≈ 4.4 天才能完全修正，所以偏差必須在小時就被發現。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: If the core is found 20 mm off line and corrected at a gradient of 1:500, the correction height is 20 mm×500 = 10 m; at 2.29 m per day that takes about 10/2.29 ≈ 4.4 days, so deviations must be caught while still small. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以雷射垂準儀從底部基準點向平台上的接收靶投點，每班至少量測兩次並記錄 x、y 偏移與平台扭轉角；平台水平以水管水準或數位傾斜計監測，量測值超過警戒值時由滑模工程師下達修正指令。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Project from base reference points to targets on the deck with laser plumbs at least twice per shift, recording x and y offsets and deck rotation; monitor deck level with water levels or digital inclinometers, and have the slipform engineer issue correction instructions when readings exceed the alert value.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"若量到核心筒偏離 20 mm，以 1:500 的修正坡度拉回，需要的修正高度 = 20 mm×500 = 10 m；日升 2.29 m 時約需 10/2.29 ≈ 4.4 天才能完全修正，所以偏差必須在小時就被發現。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"If the core is found 20 mm off line and corrected at a gradient of 1:500, the correction height is 20 mm×500 = 10 m; at 2.29 m per day that takes about 10/2.29 ≈ 4.4 days, so deviations must be caught while still small. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「垂直度、扭轉與平台水平的修正」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Correcting verticality, twist and deck level\", which statement holds?","options":["若量到核心筒偏離 20 mm，以 1:500 的修正坡度拉回，需要的修正高度 = 20 mm×500 = 10 m。","自動化液壓系統會讓所有千斤頂完全同步，不需要人工量測。","核心筒驗收只要總高度與整體垂直度合格就足夠。"],"optionsEn":["If the core is found 20 mm off line and corrected at a gradient of 1:500, the correction height is 20 mm×500 = 10 m.","Automated hydraulics keep every jack perfectly synchronised, so manual levelling is unnecessary.","A core passes acceptance if its total height and overall verticality are within tolerance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若量到核心筒偏離 20 mm，以 1:500 的修正坡度拉回，需要的修正高度 = 20 mm×500 = 10 m；日升 2.29 m 時約需 10/2.29 ≈ 4.4 天才能完全修正，所以偏差必須在小時就被發現。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"If the core is found 20 mm off line and corrected at a gradient of 1:500, the correction height is 20 mm×500 = 10 m; at 2.29 m per day that takes about 10/2.29 ≈ 4.4 days, so deviations must be caught while still small. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b061-v13-19","title":"垂直度、扭轉與平台水平的修正：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Correcting verticality, twist and deck level: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「垂直度與扭轉控制」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Verticality and twist control” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以雷射垂準儀從底部基準點向平台上的接收靶投點，每班至少量測兩次並記錄 x、y 偏移與平台扭轉角；平台水平以水管水準或數位傾斜計監測，量測值超過警戒值時由滑模工程師下達修正指令。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Project from base reference points to targets on the deck with laser plumbs at least twice per shift, recording x and y offsets and deck rotation; monitor deck level with water levels or digital inclinometers, and have the slipform engineer issue correction instructions when readings exceed the alert value. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：測量紀錄應繪成隨高度變化的偏差曲線並張貼在平台上，讓各班看到趨勢而非單點數值；修正指令與執行結果都寫入滑升日誌，由測量主管與滑模工程師簽記。","observationEn":"Site practice: Plot survey results as deviation-versus-height curves posted on the deck so each shift sees the trend rather than a single reading; write correction instructions and their results into the slip log, signed by the survey lead and the slipform engineer.","failure":"注意干擾：發現偏差後一次大幅傾斜模板強行修正，牆面出現明顯折角與水平裂縫，電梯導軌安裝困難；長期忽略平台扭轉，核心筒逐層旋轉，與外圍樓板鋼梁連接位置錯開。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Forcing a large single correction by tilting the forms leaves visible kinks and horizontal cracks in the wall and makes elevator rail installation difficult; ignoring deck twist for long lets the core rotate storey by storey so that connections to perimeter floor beams no longer line up. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以雷射垂準儀從底部基準點向平台上的接收靶投點，每班至少量測兩次並記錄 x、y 偏移與平台扭轉角；平台水平以水管水準或數位傾斜計監測，量測值超過警戒值時由滑模工程師下達修正指令。","textEn":"Project from base reference points to targets on the deck with laser plumbs at least twice per shift, recording x and y offsets and deck rotation; monitor deck level with water levels or digital inclinometers, and have the slipform engineer issue correction instructions when readings exceed the alert value.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"測量紀錄應繪成隨高度變化的偏差曲線並張貼在平台上，讓各班看到趨勢而非單點數值；修正指令與執行結果都寫入滑升日誌，由測量主管與滑模工程師簽記。","textEn":"Plot survey results as deviation-versus-height curves posted on the deck so each shift sees the trend rather than a single reading; write correction instructions and their results into the slip log, signed by the survey lead and the slipform engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「垂直度、扭轉與平台水平的修正」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Correcting verticality, twist and deck level\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以雷射垂準儀從底部基準點向平台上的接收靶投點，每班至少量測兩次並記錄 x、y 偏移與平台扭轉角。","滑模的速度越快越好，只要千斤頂能力足夠就可以一直加速。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Project from base reference points to targets on the deck with laser plumbs at least twice per shift, recording x and y offsets and deck rotation.","The faster the slipform the better; it can keep accelerating as long as the jacks are strong enough."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以雷射垂準儀從底部基準點向平台上的接收靶投點，每班至少量測兩次並記錄 x、y 偏移與平台扭轉角；平台水平以水管水準或數位傾斜計監測，量測值超過警戒值時由滑模工程師下達修正指令。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Project from base reference points to targets on the deck with laser plumbs at least twice per shift, recording x and y offsets and deck rotation; monitor deck level with water levels or digital inclinometers, and have the slipform engineer issue correction instructions when readings exceed the alert value. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b061-v13-20","title":"垂直度、扭轉與平台水平的修正：失效診斷","titleEn":"Correcting verticality, twist and deck level: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「垂直度與扭轉控制」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Verticality and twist control” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"發現偏差後一次大幅傾斜模板強行修正，牆面出現明顯折角與水平裂縫，電梯導軌安裝困難；長期忽略平台扭轉，核心筒逐層旋轉，與外圍樓板鋼梁連接位置錯開。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Forcing a large single correction by tilting the forms leaves visible kinks and horizontal cracks in the wall and makes elevator rail installation difficult; ignoring deck twist for long lets the core rotate storey by storey so that connections to perimeter floor beams no longer line up. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：亞特蘭大試驗塔的牆面垂直偏差控制在約 ±6 mm（±¼ in）以內。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: At the Atlanta test tower the vertical surface deviation was held within about ±6 mm (±¼ in).","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「滑模偏了只要在下一段一次調回原位即可。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"If the slipform drifts, it can simply be returned to position in the next lift.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"發現偏差後一次大幅傾斜模板強行修正，牆面出現明顯折角與水平裂縫，電梯導軌安裝困難；長期忽略平台扭轉，核心筒逐層旋轉，與外圍樓板鋼梁連接位置錯開。","textEn":"Forcing a large single correction by tilting the forms leaves visible kinks and horizontal cracks in the wall and makes elevator rail installation difficult; ignoring deck twist for long lets the core rotate storey by storey so that connections to perimeter floor beams no longer line up.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「垂直度、扭轉與平台水平的修正」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Correcting verticality, twist and deck level\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","滑模混凝土是連續澆置的，所以牆內不會有施工縫。","發現偏差後一次大幅傾斜模板強行修正，牆面出現明顯折角與水平裂縫，電梯導軌安裝困難；長期忽略平台扭轉，核心筒逐層旋轉，與外圍樓板鋼梁連接位置錯開。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Slipformed walls are cast continuously, so they never contain construction joints.","Forcing a large single correction by tilting the forms leaves visible kinks and horizontal cracks in the wall and makes elevator rail installation difficult."],"answer":2,"explanation":"發現偏差後一次大幅傾斜模板強行修正，牆面出現明顯折角與水平裂縫，電梯導軌安裝困難；長期忽略平台扭轉，核心筒逐層旋轉，與外圍樓板鋼梁連接位置錯開。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Forcing a large single correction by tilting the forms leaves visible kinks and horizontal cracks in the wall and makes elevator rail installation difficult; ignoring deck twist for long lets the core rotate storey by storey so that connections to perimeter floor beams no longer line up. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b061-v13-21","title":"計畫停機、冷縫處理與惡劣天候：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Planned stops, cold joints and bad weather: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「計畫停機與冷縫」如何影響高層建築核心筒滑模施工的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Planned stops and cold joints” governs force, deformation or durability in “Slipform construction of high-rise cores”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"滑模雖以連續作業為原則，但遇到樓層大改變、設備維修、強風或供料中斷，仍需要停機。停機時要讓模板內混凝土澆到預定高程並持續以小行程「鬆模」，避免混凝土與模板黏結；重新啟動前則要把接縫面打毛、清潔與濕潤，形成可傳遞剪力的施工縫。亞特蘭大試驗塔 24 小時連續作業，期間安排了三次各約一天的停機，並在這些位置形成冷縫。冷縫是剪力牆受力的薄弱面，必須按剪力摩擦檢核。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「計畫停機與冷縫」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Although slipforming aims to be continuous, major changes of section, equipment maintenance, strong winds or supply interruptions still force stops. When stopping, concrete is brought to a planned level and the forms are jogged in small strokes to keep concrete from bonding to them; before restarting, the joint surface is roughened, cleaned and wetted to form a construction joint that can transfer shear. The Atlanta test tower worked 24 hours a day with three planned stops of about a day each, which formed cold joints at those levels. A cold joint is a weak plane in a shear wall and must be checked by shear friction. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Planned stops and cold joints” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：剪力摩擦 V_n = μ·A_vf·f_y。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Shear friction V_n = μ·A_vf·f_y.","failure":"常見誤解：「滑模混凝土是連續澆置的，所以牆內不會有施工縫。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Slipformed walls are cast continuously, so they never contain construction joints.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「計畫停機與冷縫」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Planned stops and cold joints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-21-k1","title":"計畫停機、冷縫處理與惡劣天候","titleEn":"Planned stops, cold joints and bad weather","text":"滑模雖以連續作業為原則，但遇到樓層大改變、設備維修、強風或供料中斷，仍需要停機。停機時要讓模板內混凝土澆到預定高程並持續以小行程「鬆模」，避免混凝土與模板黏結；重新啟動前則要把接縫面打毛、清潔與濕潤，形成可傳遞剪力的施工縫。","textEn":"Although slipforming aims to be continuous, major changes of section, equipment maintenance, strong winds or supply interruptions still force stops. When stopping, concrete is brought to a planned level and the forms are jogged in small strokes to keep concrete from bonding to them; before restarting, the joint surface is roughened, cleaned and wetted to form a construction joint that can transfer shear.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：滑模混凝土是連續澆置的，所以牆內不會有施工縫。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Slipformed walls are cast continuously, so they never contain construction joints. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「計畫停機、冷縫處理與惡劣天候」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Planned stops, cold joints and bad weather\" is correct?","options":["滑模雖以連續作業為原則，但遇到樓層大改變、設備維修、強風或供料中斷，仍需要停機。","滑模混凝土是連續澆置的，所以牆內不會有施工縫。","混凝土在模板內放滿固定小時數就一定可以出模，與溫度無關。"],"optionsEn":["Although slipforming aims to be continuous, major changes of section, equipment maintenance, strong winds or supply interruptions still force stops.","Slipformed walls are cast continuously, so they never contain construction joints.","Concrete can always leave the form after a fixed number of hours regardless of temperature."],"answer":0,"explanation":"滑模雖以連續作業為原則，但遇到樓層大改變、設備維修、強風或供料中斷，仍需要停機。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Although slipforming aims to be continuous, major changes of section, equipment maintenance, strong winds or supply interruptions still force stops. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b061-v13-22","title":"計畫停機、冷縫處理與惡劣天候：定量估算","titleEn":"Planned stops, cold joints and bad weather: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「計畫停機與冷縫」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Planned stops and cold joints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：剪力摩擦 V_n = μ·A_vf·f_y。垂直筋 φ16@200 雙面，A_vf = 2×201/0.2 = 2,010 mm²/m；f_y = 420 MPa；接縫打毛 μ = 1.0 時 φV_n = 0.75×1.0×2,010×420 ≈ 633 kN/m，大於需求 500 kN/m；若未打毛 μ = 0.6，φV_n ≈ 380 kN/m，不足。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Shear friction V_n = μ·A_vf·f_y. Vertical bars φ16 at 200 mm on both faces give A_vf = 2×201/0.2 = 2,010 mm²/m; with f_y = 420 MPa and a roughened joint μ = 1.0, φV_n = 0.75×1.0×2,010×420 ≈ 633 kN/m, above a demand of 500 kN/m; an unroughened joint with μ = 0.6 gives φV_n ≈ 380 kN/m, which is insufficient. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：停機前後各拍攝接縫面照片並量測打毛深度（例如以砂填法或深度規），重新澆置前檢查接縫是否清潔濕潤；冷縫位置與處理方式要記錄高程，並由結構設計者確認該位置的剪力需求與摩擦係數假設相符。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Photograph the joint before and after the stop and measure roughness amplitude with a sand-patch method or depth gauge; before restarting check that the joint is clean and damp; record the elevation and treatment of each cold joint and have the structural designer confirm that the shear demand there matches the friction coefficient assumed.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"剪力摩擦 V_n = μ·A_vf·f_y。垂直筋 φ16@200 雙面，A_vf = 2×201/0.2 = 2,010 mm²/m；f_y = 420 MPa；接縫打毛 μ = 1.0 時 φV_n = 0.75×1.0×2,010×420 ≈ 633 kN/m，大於需求 500 kN/m；若未打毛 μ = 0.6，φV_n ≈ 380 kN/m，不足。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Shear friction V_n = μ·A_vf·f_y. Vertical bars φ16 at 200 mm on both faces give A_vf = 2×201/0.2 = 2,010 mm²/m; with f_y = 420 MPa and a roughened joint μ = 1.0, φV_n = 0.75×1.0×2,010×420 ≈ 633 kN/m, above a demand of 500 kN/m; an unroughened joint with μ = 0.6 gives φV_n ≈ 380 kN/m, which is insufficient. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「計畫停機、冷縫處理與惡劣天候」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Planned stops, cold joints and bad weather\", which statement holds?","options":["核心筒以後會被裝修包覆，所以滑模牆面的養護不重要。","剪力摩擦 V_n = μ·A_vf·f_y。","滑模適用於所有高層核心筒，只要速度夠快就一定比較省工期。"],"optionsEn":["Core walls will be covered by finishes later, so curing slipformed surfaces does not matter.","Shear friction V_n = μ·A_vf·f_y.","Slipforming suits every high-rise core and is always faster if the rate is high enough."],"answer":1,"explanation":"剪力摩擦 V_n = μ·A_vf·f_y。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Shear friction V_n = μ·A_vf·f_y. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b061-v13-23","title":"計畫停機、冷縫處理與惡劣天候：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Planned stops, cold joints and bad weather: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「計畫停機與冷縫」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Planned stops and cold joints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"停機前後各拍攝接縫面照片並量測打毛深度（例如以砂填法或深度規），重新澆置前檢查接縫是否清潔濕潤；冷縫位置與處理方式要記錄高程，並由結構設計者確認該位置的剪力需求與摩擦係數假設相符。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Photograph the joint before and after the stop and measure roughness amplitude with a sand-patch method or depth gauge; before restarting check that the joint is clean and damp; record the elevation and treatment of each cold joint and have the structural designer confirm that the shear demand there matches the friction coefficient assumed. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：施工計畫要預先規劃停機高程（避開高剪力區與埋件密集區），並備妥非預期停機的應變程序：鬆模頻率、停止澆置高程、接縫處理與重啟檢查，由滑模工程師負責下令。","observationEn":"Site practice: Plan stop elevations in advance, away from high-shear zones and dense embed bands, and prepare a contingency procedure for unplanned stops covering jogging frequency, the level at which pouring stops, joint treatment and restart checks, with the slipform engineer responsible for giving the orders.","failure":"注意干擾：未預期的停機沒有鬆模，模板與混凝土黏死，重啟時強拉撕裂牆面；冷縫未打毛就續澆，接縫成為光滑弱面，地震或強風下沿縫滑移並滲水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An unplanned stop without jogging locks the forms to the concrete and restarting tears the wall; continuing over an unroughened cold joint leaves a smooth weak plane that can slip and leak under earthquake or strong wind. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"停機前後各拍攝接縫面照片並量測打毛深度（例如以砂填法或深度規），重新澆置前檢查接縫是否清潔濕潤；冷縫位置與處理方式要記錄高程，並由結構設計者確認該位置的剪力需求與摩擦係數假設相符。","textEn":"Photograph the joint before and after the stop and measure roughness amplitude with a sand-patch method or depth gauge; before restarting check that the joint is clean and damp; record the elevation and treatment of each cold joint and have the structural designer confirm that the shear demand there matches the friction coefficient assumed.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"施工計畫要預先規劃停機高程（避開高剪力區與埋件密集區），並備妥非預期停機的應變程序：鬆模頻率、停止澆置高程、接縫處理與重啟檢查，由滑模工程師負責下令。","textEn":"Plan stop elevations in advance, away from high-shear zones and dense embed bands, and prepare a contingency procedure for unplanned stops covering jogging frequency, the level at which pouring stops, joint treatment and restart checks, with the slipform engineer responsible for giving the orders.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「計畫停機、冷縫處理與惡劣天候」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Planned stops, cold joints and bad weather\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","千斤頂額定荷重夠大，就代表爬桿與平台一定安全。","停機前後各拍攝接縫面照片並量測打毛深度（例如以砂填法或深度規），重新澆置前檢查接縫是否清潔濕潤。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","If the jack rating is high enough, the rods and deck must be safe.","Photograph the joint before and after the stop and measure roughness amplitude with a sand-patch method or depth gauge."],"answer":2,"explanation":"停機前後各拍攝接縫面照片並量測打毛深度（例如以砂填法或深度規），重新澆置前檢查接縫是否清潔濕潤；冷縫位置與處理方式要記錄高程，並由結構設計者確認該位置的剪力需求與摩擦係數假設相符。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Photograph the joint before and after the stop and measure roughness amplitude with a sand-patch method or depth gauge; before restarting check that the joint is clean and damp; record the elevation and treatment of each cold joint and have the structural designer confirm that the shear demand there matches the friction coefficient assumed. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b061-v13-24","title":"計畫停機、冷縫處理與惡劣天候：失效診斷","titleEn":"Planned stops, cold joints and bad weather: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「計畫停機與冷縫」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Planned stops and cold joints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"未預期的停機沒有鬆模，模板與混凝土黏死，重啟時強拉撕裂牆面；冷縫未打毛就續澆，接縫成為光滑弱面，地震或強風下沿縫滑移並滲水。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An unplanned stop without jogging locks the forms to the concrete and restarting tears the wall; continuing over an unroughened cold joint leaves a smooth weak plane that can slip and leak under earthquake or strong wind. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：冷縫是剪力牆受力的薄弱面，必須按剪力摩擦檢核。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A cold joint is a weak plane in a shear wall and must be checked by shear friction.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「滑模混凝土是連續澆置的，所以牆內不會有施工縫。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Slipformed walls are cast continuously, so they never contain construction joints.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"未預期的停機沒有鬆模，模板與混凝土黏死，重啟時強拉撕裂牆面；冷縫未打毛就續澆，接縫成為光滑弱面，地震或強風下沿縫滑移並滲水。","textEn":"An unplanned stop without jogging locks the forms to the concrete and restarting tears the wall; continuing over an unroughened cold joint leaves a smooth weak plane that can slip and leak under earthquake or strong wind.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「計畫停機、冷縫處理與惡劣天候」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Planned stops, cold joints and bad weather\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["未預期的停機沒有鬆模，模板與混凝土黏死，重啟時強拉撕裂牆面；冷縫未打毛就續澆，接縫成為光滑弱面，地震或強風下沿縫滑移並滲水。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","混凝土在模板內放滿固定小時數就一定可以出模，與溫度無關。"],"optionsEn":["An unplanned stop without jogging locks the forms to the concrete and restarting tears the wall.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Concrete can always leave the form after a fixed number of hours regardless of temperature."],"answer":0,"explanation":"未預期的停機沒有鬆模，模板與混凝土黏死，重啟時強拉撕裂牆面；冷縫未打毛就續澆，接縫成為光滑弱面，地震或強風下沿縫滑移並滲水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An unplanned stop without jogging locks the forms to the concrete and restarting tears the wall; continuing over an unroughened cold joint leaves a smooth weak plane that can slip and leak under earthquake or strong wind. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b061-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「出模檢查、早齡強度與成熟度法」與「千斤頂同步、平台水平量測與滑升日誌」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Exit checks, early-age strength and the maturity method\" and \"Jack synchronisation, deck levelling and the slip log\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b061-v13-25","title":"出模檢查、早齡強度與成熟度法：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Exit checks, early-age strength and the maturity method: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「出模面檢查與成熟度」如何影響高層建築核心筒滑模施工的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Exit-surface checks and maturity” governs force, deformation or durability in “Slipform construction of high-rise cores”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"滑模每天要決定好幾次速度，不可能每次等試體壓驗結果，所以實務上同時使用即時檢查與預測方法：出模面的手壓或貫入檢查、溫度感測器配合成熟度法估計早齡強度，以及定期的標準試體作最終驗收。成熟度法假設同一配比在相同溫度—時間累積下會達到相同強度，因此先在試驗室建立成熟度與強度曲線，現場只要量測混凝土溫度就能推估強度。這對日夜溫差大或冬季施工尤其重要。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「出模面檢查與成熟度」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A slipform needs speed decisions several times a day and cannot wait for cylinder results each time, so practice combines immediate checks with prediction: thumb or penetration checks at the exit surface, temperature sensors with the maturity method to estimate early strength, and standard cylinders for final acceptance. The maturity method assumes that a given mix reaches the same strength at the same accumulated temperature–time, so a laboratory maturity–strength curve is built first and site strength is then estimated from concrete temperature alone. This matters most with large day–night swings or winter work. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Exit-surface checks and maturity” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：Nurse–Saul 成熟度 M = Σ(T − T₀)Δt，基準溫度 T₀ = −10°C。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Nurse–Saul maturity M = Σ(T − T₀)Δt with datum T₀ = −10°C.","failure":"常見誤解：「混凝土在模板內放滿固定小時數就一定可以出模，與溫度無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Concrete can always leave the form after a fixed number of hours regardless of temperature.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「出模面檢查與成熟度」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Exit-surface checks and maturity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-25-k1","title":"出模檢查、早齡強度與成熟度法","titleEn":"Exit checks, early-age strength and the maturity method","text":"滑模每天要決定好幾次速度，不可能每次等試體壓驗結果，所以實務上同時使用即時檢查與預測方法：出模面的手壓或貫入檢查、溫度感測器配合成熟度法估計早齡強度，以及定期的標準試體作最終驗收。成熟度法假設同一配比在相同溫度—時間累積下會達到相同強度，因此先在試驗室建立成熟度與強度曲線，現場只要量測混凝土溫度就能推估強度。","textEn":"A slipform needs speed decisions several times a day and cannot wait for cylinder results each time, so practice combines immediate checks with prediction: thumb or penetration checks at the exit surface, temperature sensors with the maturity method to estimate early strength, and standard cylinders for final acceptance. The maturity method assumes that a given mix reaches the same strength at the same accumulated temperature–time, so a laboratory maturity–strength curve is built first and site strength is then estimated from concrete temperature alone.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：混凝土在模板內放滿固定小時數就一定可以出模，與溫度無關。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Concrete can always leave the form after a fixed number of hours regardless of temperature. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「出模檢查、早齡強度與成熟度法」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Exit checks, early-age strength and the maturity method\" is correct?","options":["混凝土在模板內放滿固定小時數就一定可以出模，與溫度無關。","滑模每天要決定好幾次速度，不可能每次等試體壓驗結果，所以實務上同時使用即時檢查與預測方法：出模面的手壓或貫入檢查、溫度感測器配合成熟度法估計早齡強度，以及定期的標準試體作最終驗收。","自動化液壓系統會讓所有千斤頂完全同步，不需要人工量測。"],"optionsEn":["Concrete can always leave the form after a fixed number of hours regardless of temperature.","A slipform needs speed decisions several times a day and cannot wait for cylinder results each time, so practice combines immediate checks with prediction: thumb or penetration checks at the exit surface, temperature sensors with the maturity method to estimate early strength, and standard cylinders for final acceptance.","Automated hydraulics keep every jack perfectly synchronised, so manual levelling is unnecessary."],"answer":1,"explanation":"滑模每天要決定好幾次速度，不可能每次等試體壓驗結果，所以實務上同時使用即時檢查與預測方法：出模面的手壓或貫入檢查、溫度感測器配合成熟度法估計早齡強度，以及定期的標準試體作最終驗收。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A slipform needs speed decisions several times a day and cannot wait for cylinder results each time, so practice combines immediate checks with prediction: thumb or penetration checks at the exit surface, temperature sensors with the maturity method to estimate early strength, and standard cylinders for final acceptance. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b061-v13-26","title":"出模檢查、早齡強度與成熟度法：定量估算","titleEn":"Exit checks, early-age strength and the maturity method: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「出模面檢查與成熟度」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Exit-surface checks and maturity” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：Nurse–Saul 成熟度 M = Σ(T − T₀)Δt，基準溫度 T₀ = −10°C。20°C 時 10 h 累積 30×10 = 300 °C·h；若出模所需成熟度為 300 °C·h，10°C 時需 300/20 = 15 h。模板有效高度 1.0 m，容許速度由 0.10 m/h 降為 1.0/15 ≈ 0.067 m/h。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Nurse–Saul maturity M = Σ(T − T₀)Δt with datum T₀ = −10°C. Ten hours at 20°C accumulate 30×10 = 300 °C·h; if exit requires 300 °C·h, at 10°C it takes 300/20 = 15 h. With 1.0 m effective form height the rate must fall from 0.10 m/h to 1.0/15 ≈ 0.067 m/h. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：開工前以同一配比在試驗室建立成熟度—強度曲線，並以現場早期試體驗證；滑升中在模板下緣附近埋設溫度感測器，每小時計算成熟度，與出模面手壓檢查結果互相印證，最終強度以標準養護試體驗收。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build the maturity–strength curve for the mix in the laboratory before starting and validate it with early site specimens; during sliding embed temperature sensors near the form bottom, compute maturity hourly and cross-check with exit-surface thumb tests, while final acceptance rests on standard-cured cylinders.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"Nurse–Saul 成熟度 M = Σ(T − T₀)Δt，基準溫度 T₀ = −10°C。20°C 時 10 h 累積 30×10 = 300 °C·h；若出模所需成熟度為 300 °C·h，10°C 時需 300/20 = 15 h。模板有效高度 1.0 m，容許速度由 0.10 m/h 降為 1.0/15 ≈ 0.067 m/h。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Nurse–Saul maturity M = Σ(T − T₀)Δt with datum T₀ = −10°C. Ten hours at 20°C accumulate 30×10 = 300 °C·h; if exit requires 300 °C·h, at 10°C it takes 300/20 = 15 h. With 1.0 m effective form height the rate must fall from 0.10 m/h to 1.0/15 ≈ 0.067 m/h. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「出模檢查、早齡強度與成熟度法」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Exit checks, early-age strength and the maturity method\", which statement holds?","options":["核心筒驗收只要總高度與整體垂直度合格就足夠。","滑模的速度越快越好，只要千斤頂能力足夠就可以一直加速。","Nurse–Saul 成熟度 M = Σ(T − T₀)Δt，基準溫度 T₀ = −10°C。"],"optionsEn":["A core passes acceptance if its total height and overall verticality are within tolerance.","The faster the slipform the better; it can keep accelerating as long as the jacks are strong enough.","Nurse–Saul maturity M = Σ(T − T₀)Δt with datum T₀ = −10°C."],"answer":2,"explanation":"Nurse–Saul 成熟度 M = Σ(T − T₀)Δt，基準溫度 T₀ = −10°C。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Nurse–Saul maturity M = Σ(T − T₀)Δt with datum T₀ = −10°C. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b061-v13-27","title":"出模檢查、早齡強度與成熟度法：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Exit checks, early-age strength and the maturity method: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「出模面檢查與成熟度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Exit-surface checks and maturity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"開工前以同一配比在試驗室建立成熟度—強度曲線，並以現場早期試體驗證；滑升中在模板下緣附近埋設溫度感測器，每小時計算成熟度，與出模面手壓檢查結果互相印證，最終強度以標準養護試體驗收。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build the maturity–strength curve for the mix in the laboratory before starting and validate it with early site specimens; during sliding embed temperature sensors near the form bottom, compute maturity hourly and cross-check with exit-surface thumb tests, while final acceptance rests on standard-cured cylinders. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：任何配比、水泥或摻料來源變更都要重新建立或驗證成熟度曲線；感測器位置與遮蔽方式寫入品質計畫，資料自動上傳並設警戒值，夜班也能即時看到強度推估。","observationEn":"Site practice: Re-establish or validate the maturity curve after any change of mix, cement or admixture source; write sensor positions and shielding into the quality plan, upload data automatically with alert thresholds so the night shift sees strength estimates in real time.","failure":"注意干擾：配比中途更換水泥來源卻沿用舊的成熟度曲線，推估強度偏高，出模混凝土實際太軟而坍落；感測器裝在受陽光直射的位置，讀到的溫度偏高，同樣導致高估強度。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Changing the cement source mid-job while keeping the old maturity curve overestimates strength, so concrete leaves the form too soft and slumps; sensors placed in direct sun read high temperatures and likewise overestimate strength. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"開工前以同一配比在試驗室建立成熟度—強度曲線，並以現場早期試體驗證；滑升中在模板下緣附近埋設溫度感測器，每小時計算成熟度，與出模面手壓檢查結果互相印證，最終強度以標準養護試體驗收。","textEn":"Build the maturity–strength curve for the mix in the laboratory before starting and validate it with early site specimens; during sliding embed temperature sensors near the form bottom, compute maturity hourly and cross-check with exit-surface thumb tests, while final acceptance rests on standard-cured cylinders.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"任何配比、水泥或摻料來源變更都要重新建立或驗證成熟度曲線；感測器位置與遮蔽方式寫入品質計畫，資料自動上傳並設警戒值，夜班也能即時看到強度推估。","textEn":"Re-establish or validate the maturity curve after any change of mix, cement or admixture source; write sensor positions and shielding into the quality plan, upload data automatically with alert thresholds so the night shift sees strength estimates in real time.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「出模檢查、早齡強度與成熟度法」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Exit checks, early-age strength and the maturity method\"?","options":["開工前以同一配比在試驗室建立成熟度—強度曲線，並以現場早期試體驗證。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","滑模速度快，所以埋件位置可以完工後再用鑽孔方式補做。"],"optionsEn":["Build the maturity–strength curve for the mix in the laboratory before starting and validate it with early site specimens.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Because slipforming is fast, embed positions can be added afterwards by drilling."],"answer":0,"explanation":"開工前以同一配比在試驗室建立成熟度—強度曲線，並以現場早期試體驗證；滑升中在模板下緣附近埋設溫度感測器，每小時計算成熟度，與出模面手壓檢查結果互相印證，最終強度以標準養護試體驗收。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build the maturity–strength curve for the mix in the laboratory before starting and validate it with early site specimens; during sliding embed temperature sensors near the form bottom, compute maturity hourly and cross-check with exit-surface thumb tests, while final acceptance rests on standard-cured cylinders. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b061-v13-28","title":"出模檢查、早齡強度與成熟度法：失效診斷","titleEn":"Exit checks, early-age strength and the maturity method: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「出模面檢查與成熟度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Exit-surface checks and maturity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"配比中途更換水泥來源卻沿用舊的成熟度曲線，推估強度偏高，出模混凝土實際太軟而坍落；感測器裝在受陽光直射的位置，讀到的溫度偏高，同樣導致高估強度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Changing the cement source mid-job while keeping the old maturity curve overestimates strength, so concrete leaves the form too soft and slumps; sensors placed in direct sun read high temperatures and likewise overestimate strength. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這對日夜溫差大或冬季施工尤其重要。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: This matters most with large day–night swings or winter work.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「混凝土在模板內放滿固定小時數就一定可以出模，與溫度無關。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Concrete can always leave the form after a fixed number of hours regardless of temperature.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"配比中途更換水泥來源卻沿用舊的成熟度曲線，推估強度偏高，出模混凝土實際太軟而坍落；感測器裝在受陽光直射的位置，讀到的溫度偏高，同樣導致高估強度。","textEn":"Changing the cement source mid-job while keeping the old maturity curve overestimates strength, so concrete leaves the form too soft and slumps; sensors placed in direct sun read high temperatures and likewise overestimate strength.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「出模檢查、早齡強度與成熟度法」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Exit checks, early-age strength and the maturity method\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","配比中途更換水泥來源卻沿用舊的成熟度曲線，推估強度偏高，出模混凝土實際太軟而坍落；感測器裝在受陽光直射的位置，讀到的溫度偏高，同樣導致高估強度。","自動化液壓系統會讓所有千斤頂完全同步，不需要人工量測。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Changing the cement source mid-job while keeping the old maturity curve overestimates strength, so concrete leaves the form too soft and slumps.","Automated hydraulics keep every jack perfectly synchronised, so manual levelling is unnecessary."],"answer":1,"explanation":"配比中途更換水泥來源卻沿用舊的成熟度曲線，推估強度偏高，出模混凝土實際太軟而坍落；感測器裝在受陽光直射的位置，讀到的溫度偏高，同樣導致高估強度。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Changing the cement source mid-job while keeping the old maturity curve overestimates strength, so concrete leaves the form too soft and slumps; sensors placed in direct sun read high temperatures and likewise overestimate strength. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b061-v13-29","title":"千斤頂同步、平台水平量測與滑升日誌：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Jack synchronisation, deck levelling and the slip log: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「平台水平與千斤頂同步」如何影響高層建築核心筒滑模施工的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Deck level and jack synchronisation” governs force, deformation or durability in “Slipform construction of high-rise cores”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"滑模平台由數十支千斤頂同時推升，每支每一行程只上升數十毫米；只要部分千斤頂行程略短，平台就會逐漸傾斜。現代滑模以集中油壓與水平感測自動控制，但仍需人員定期量測並調整。滑升日誌是滑模的「黑盒子」：記錄每小時的高程、速度、混凝土溫度與供料、千斤頂狀況、偏差量測、停機與修正，日後若牆體出現問題，可以追溯到當時的作業條件。亞特蘭大試驗塔的千斤頂約每 15 分鐘把平台頂升約 25 mm（1 in）。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「平台水平與千斤頂同步」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Dozens of jacks lift the deck together, each stroke only tens of millimetres; if some jacks stroke slightly short, the deck gradually tilts. Modern slipforms use central hydraulics with level sensing and automatic control, yet people must still measure and adjust regularly. The slip log is the slipform's black box: it records hourly level, rate, concrete temperature and supply, jack condition, deviation readings, stops and corrections, so that any later problem in the wall can be traced to the conditions at the time. At the Atlanta test tower the jacks lifted the deck about 25 mm (1 in) roughly every 15 minutes. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Deck level and jack synchronisation” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：千斤頂行程 25 mm，若某群組每行程少 1 mm，10 個行程後高差 10 mm；平台寬 22 m 時傾斜 10/22,000 ≈ 1:2,200。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: With a 25 mm jack stroke, a group that falls 1 mm short per stroke is 10 mm low after 10 strokes; across a 22 m deck that is a tilt of 10/22,000 ≈ 1:2,200.","failure":"常見誤解：「自動化液壓系統會讓所有千斤頂完全同步，不需要人工量測。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Automated hydraulics keep every jack perfectly synchronised, so manual levelling is unnecessary.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「平台水平與千斤頂同步」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Deck level and jack synchronisation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-29-k1","title":"千斤頂同步、平台水平量測與滑升日誌","titleEn":"Jack synchronisation, deck levelling and the slip log","text":"滑模平台由數十支千斤頂同時推升，每支每一行程只上升數十毫米；只要部分千斤頂行程略短，平台就會逐漸傾斜。現代滑模以集中油壓與水平感測自動控制，但仍需人員定期量測並調整。","textEn":"Dozens of jacks lift the deck together, each stroke only tens of millimetres; if some jacks stroke slightly short, the deck gradually tilts. Modern slipforms use central hydraulics with level sensing and automatic control, yet people must still measure and adjust regularly.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：自動化液壓系統會讓所有千斤頂完全同步，不需要人工量測。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Automated hydraulics keep every jack perfectly synchronised, so manual levelling is unnecessary. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「千斤頂同步、平台水平量測與滑升日誌」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Jack synchronisation, deck levelling and the slip log\" is correct?","options":["自動化液壓系統會讓所有千斤頂完全同步，不需要人工量測。","核心筒以後會被裝修包覆，所以滑模牆面的養護不重要。","滑模平台由數十支千斤頂同時推升，每支每一行程只上升數十毫米；只要部分千斤頂行程略短，平台就會逐漸傾斜。"],"optionsEn":["Automated hydraulics keep every jack perfectly synchronised, so manual levelling is unnecessary.","Core walls will be covered by finishes later, so curing slipformed surfaces does not matter.","Dozens of jacks lift the deck together, each stroke only tens of millimetres; if some jacks stroke slightly short, the deck gradually tilts."],"answer":2,"explanation":"滑模平台由數十支千斤頂同時推升，每支每一行程只上升數十毫米；只要部分千斤頂行程略短，平台就會逐漸傾斜。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Dozens of jacks lift the deck together, each stroke only tens of millimetres; if some jacks stroke slightly short, the deck gradually tilts. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b061-v13-30","title":"千斤頂同步、平台水平量測與滑升日誌：定量估算","titleEn":"Jack synchronisation, deck levelling and the slip log: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「平台水平與千斤頂同步」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Deck level and jack synchronisation” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：千斤頂行程 25 mm，若某群組每行程少 1 mm，10 個行程後高差 10 mm；平台寬 22 m 時傾斜 10/22,000 ≈ 1:2,200。若規定平台高差警戒值為 15 mm，相當於 15 個行程、約 375 mm 的滑升高度內就必須修正。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: With a 25 mm jack stroke, a group that falls 1 mm short per stroke is 10 mm low after 10 strokes; across a 22 m deck that is a tilt of 10/22,000 ≈ 1:2,200. With a 15 mm deck-level alert value, correction is needed within 15 strokes, about 375 mm of rise. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每班以水準儀或水管水準量測平台四角與中間點高程，與自動系統讀值比對；滑升日誌以固定格式每小時填寫，並由當班滑模主管與品管簽名，電子化日誌應自動記錄千斤頂油壓與行程計數。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Each shift level the deck corners and mid-points with an optical level or water level and compare with the automatic system; fill in the slip log hourly in a fixed format signed by the shift slipform supervisor and quality controller, and have an electronic log record jack pressures and stroke counts automatically.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"千斤頂行程 25 mm，若某群組每行程少 1 mm，10 個行程後高差 10 mm；平台寬 22 m 時傾斜 10/22,000 ≈ 1:2,200。若規定平台高差警戒值為 15 mm，相當於 15 個行程、約 375 mm 的滑升高度內就必須修正。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"With a 25 mm jack stroke, a group that falls 1 mm short per stroke is 10 mm low after 10 strokes; across a 22 m deck that is a tilt of 10/22,000 ≈ 1:2,200. With a 15 mm deck-level alert value, correction is needed within 15 strokes, about 375 mm of rise. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「千斤頂同步、平台水平量測與滑升日誌」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Jack synchronisation, deck levelling and the slip log\", which statement holds?","options":["千斤頂行程 25 mm，若某群組每行程少 1 mm，10 個行程後高差 10 mm；平台寬 22 m 時傾斜 10/22,000 ≈ 1:2,200。","滑模適用於所有高層核心筒，只要速度夠快就一定比較省工期。","千斤頂額定荷重夠大，就代表爬桿與平台一定安全。"],"optionsEn":["With a 25 mm jack stroke, a group that falls 1 mm short per stroke is 10 mm low after 10 strokes; across a 22 m deck that is a tilt of 10/22,000 ≈ 1:2,200.","Slipforming suits every high-rise core and is always faster if the rate is high enough.","If the jack rating is high enough, the rods and deck must be safe."],"answer":0,"explanation":"千斤頂行程 25 mm，若某群組每行程少 1 mm，10 個行程後高差 10 mm；平台寬 22 m 時傾斜 10/22,000 ≈ 1:2,200。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"With a 25 mm jack stroke, a group that falls 1 mm short per stroke is 10 mm low after 10 strokes; across a 22 m deck that is a tilt of 10/22,000 ≈ 1:2,200. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b061-v13-31","title":"千斤頂同步、平台水平量測與滑升日誌：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Jack synchronisation, deck levelling and the slip log: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「平台水平與千斤頂同步」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Deck level and jack synchronisation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每班以水準儀或水管水準量測平台四角與中間點高程，與自動系統讀值比對；滑升日誌以固定格式每小時填寫，並由當班滑模主管與品管簽名，電子化日誌應自動記錄千斤頂油壓與行程計數。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Each shift level the deck corners and mid-points with an optical level or water level and compare with the automatic system; fill in the slip log hourly in a fixed format signed by the shift slipform supervisor and quality controller, and have an electronic log record jack pressures and stroke counts automatically. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：滑升日誌格式要在開工前由監造核定，紀錄項目包含時間、高程、速度、溫度、坍度、車次、偏差、千斤頂異常與修正指令；日誌每日掃描備份，作為竣工資料的一部分。","observationEn":"Site practice: Have the resident engineer approve the slip-log format before starting, covering time, level, rate, temperatures, slump, truck numbers, deviations, jack faults and correction orders; scan and back up the log daily as part of the as-built record.","failure":"注意干擾：依賴自動控制而長期不做人工量測，感測器故障時平台逐漸傾斜卻無人察覺，模板扭曲並使牆厚不均；日誌缺漏或事後補寫，發生牆面缺陷時無法判斷是速度、溫度還是供料造成。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Relying on automatic control without manual checks means a failed sensor can let the deck tilt unnoticed, twisting the forms and making the wall uneven in thickness; gaps or after-the-fact entries in the log make it impossible to tell whether a defect came from rate, temperature or supply. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每班以水準儀或水管水準量測平台四角與中間點高程，與自動系統讀值比對；滑升日誌以固定格式每小時填寫，並由當班滑模主管與品管簽名，電子化日誌應自動記錄千斤頂油壓與行程計數。","textEn":"Each shift level the deck corners and mid-points with an optical level or water level and compare with the automatic system; fill in the slip log hourly in a fixed format signed by the shift slipform supervisor and quality controller, and have an electronic log record jack pressures and stroke counts automatically.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"滑升日誌格式要在開工前由監造核定，紀錄項目包含時間、高程、速度、溫度、坍度、車次、偏差、千斤頂異常與修正指令；日誌每日掃描備份，作為竣工資料的一部分。","textEn":"Have the resident engineer approve the slip-log format before starting, covering time, level, rate, temperatures, slump, truck numbers, deviations, jack faults and correction orders; scan and back up the log daily as part of the as-built record.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「千斤頂同步、平台水平量測與滑升日誌」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Jack synchronisation, deck levelling and the slip log\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","每班以水準儀或水管水準量測平台四角與中間點高程，與自動系統讀值比對。","滑模偏了只要在下一段一次調回原位即可。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Each shift level the deck corners and mid-points with an optical level or water level and compare with the automatic system.","If the slipform drifts, it can simply be returned to position in the next lift."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每班以水準儀或水管水準量測平台四角與中間點高程，與自動系統讀值比對；滑升日誌以固定格式每小時填寫，並由當班滑模主管與品管簽名，電子化日誌應自動記錄千斤頂油壓與行程計數。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Each shift level the deck corners and mid-points with an optical level or water level and compare with the automatic system; fill in the slip log hourly in a fixed format signed by the shift slipform supervisor and quality controller, and have an electronic log record jack pressures and stroke counts automatically. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b061-v13-32","title":"千斤頂同步、平台水平量測與滑升日誌：失效診斷","titleEn":"Jack synchronisation, deck levelling and the slip log: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「平台水平與千斤頂同步」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Deck level and jack synchronisation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"依賴自動控制而長期不做人工量測，感測器故障時平台逐漸傾斜卻無人察覺，模板扭曲並使牆厚不均；日誌缺漏或事後補寫，發生牆面缺陷時無法判斷是速度、溫度還是供料造成。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Relying on automatic control without manual checks means a failed sensor can let the deck tilt unnoticed, twisting the forms and making the wall uneven in thickness; gaps or after-the-fact entries in the log make it impossible to tell whether a defect came from rate, temperature or supply. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：亞特蘭大試驗塔的千斤頂約每 15 分鐘把平台頂升約 25 mm（1 in）。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: At the Atlanta test tower the jacks lifted the deck about 25 mm (1 in) roughly every 15 minutes.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「自動化液壓系統會讓所有千斤頂完全同步，不需要人工量測。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Automated hydraulics keep every jack perfectly synchronised, so manual levelling is unnecessary.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"依賴自動控制而長期不做人工量測，感測器故障時平台逐漸傾斜卻無人察覺，模板扭曲並使牆厚不均；日誌缺漏或事後補寫，發生牆面缺陷時無法判斷是速度、溫度還是供料造成。","textEn":"Relying on automatic control without manual checks means a failed sensor can let the deck tilt unnoticed, twisting the forms and making the wall uneven in thickness; gaps or after-the-fact entries in the log make it impossible to tell whether a defect came from rate, temperature or supply.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「千斤頂同步、平台水平量測與滑升日誌」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Jack synchronisation, deck levelling and the slip log\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","核心筒以後會被裝修包覆，所以滑模牆面的養護不重要。","依賴自動控制而長期不做人工量測，感測器故障時平台逐漸傾斜卻無人察覺，模板扭曲並使牆厚不均；日誌缺漏或事後補寫，發生牆面缺陷時無法判斷是速度、溫度還是供料造成。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Core walls will be covered by finishes later, so curing slipformed surfaces does not matter.","Relying on automatic control without manual checks means a failed sensor can let the deck tilt unnoticed, twisting the forms and making the wall uneven in thickness."],"answer":2,"explanation":"依賴自動控制而長期不做人工量測，感測器故障時平台逐漸傾斜卻無人察覺，模板扭曲並使牆厚不均；日誌缺漏或事後補寫，發生牆面缺陷時無法判斷是速度、溫度還是供料造成。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Relying on automatic control without manual checks means a failed sensor can let the deck tilt unnoticed, twisting the forms and making the wall uneven in thickness; gaps or after-the-fact entries in the log make it impossible to tell whether a defect came from rate, temperature or supply. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b061-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「出模後修飾、養護與耐久」與「竣工量測、偏差統計與工程交接」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Finishing, curing and durability after exit\" and \"As-built survey, deviation statistics and handover\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b061-v13-33","title":"出模後修飾、養護與耐久：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Finishing, curing and durability after exit: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「出模面修飾與養護」如何影響高層建築核心筒滑模施工的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Exit-surface finishing and curing” governs force, deformation or durability in “Slipform construction of high-rise cores”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"混凝土出模時表面仍很年輕，懸吊在平台下方的修飾架讓工人可以立即抹平小缺陷、填補小孔洞，並施加養護。高層核心筒外側常暴露在強風中，年輕混凝土表面水分蒸發極快，容易產生塑性收縮裂縫與表面粉化，降低保護層的耐久性。冬季則要防止出模混凝土受凍；亞特蘭大試驗塔在寒冷多雨的天氣下，混凝土本身的水化熱有助於維持溫度。修飾架也是人員作業區，需要護欄與防墜網。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「出模面修飾與養護」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Concrete leaving the form is very young, and finishing scaffolds hung below the deck let workers immediately float small defects, fill small holes and apply curing. The outside of a high core is often exposed to strong wind, so water evaporates very fast from young surfaces, causing plastic shrinkage cracks and dusting that reduce the durability of the cover. In winter, exiting concrete must be protected from freezing; at the Atlanta test tower, heat of hydration helped keep the concrete warm in cold, rainy weather. The finishing scaffold is also a work area that needs guardrails and fall-arrest netting. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Exit-surface finishing and curing” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：蒸發率 E = 5[(T_c+18)^2.5 − r(T_a+18)^2.5](V+4)×10⁻⁶（kg/m²/h）。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Evaporation rate E = 5[(T_c+18)^2.5 − r(T_a+18)^2.5](V+4)×10⁻⁶ in kg/m²/h.","failure":"常見誤解：「核心筒以後會被裝修包覆，所以滑模牆面的養護不重要。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Core walls will be covered by finishes later, so curing slipformed surfaces does not matter.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「出模面修飾與養護」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Exit-surface finishing and curing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-33-k1","title":"出模後修飾、養護與耐久","titleEn":"Finishing, curing and durability after exit","text":"混凝土出模時表面仍很年輕，懸吊在平台下方的修飾架讓工人可以立即抹平小缺陷、填補小孔洞，並施加養護。高層核心筒外側常暴露在強風中，年輕混凝土表面水分蒸發極快，容易產生塑性收縮裂縫與表面粉化，降低保護層的耐久性。","textEn":"Concrete leaving the form is very young, and finishing scaffolds hung below the deck let workers immediately float small defects, fill small holes and apply curing. The outside of a high core is often exposed to strong wind, so water evaporates very fast from young surfaces, causing plastic shrinkage cracks and dusting that reduce the durability of the cover.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：核心筒以後會被裝修包覆，所以滑模牆面的養護不重要。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Core walls will be covered by finishes later, so curing slipformed surfaces does not matter. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「出模後修飾、養護與耐久」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Finishing, curing and durability after exit\" is correct?","options":["混凝土出模時表面仍很年輕，懸吊在平台下方的修飾架讓工人可以立即抹平小缺陷、填補小孔洞，並施加養護。","核心筒以後會被裝修包覆，所以滑模牆面的養護不重要。","核心筒驗收只要總高度與整體垂直度合格就足夠。"],"optionsEn":["Concrete leaving the form is very young, and finishing scaffolds hung below the deck let workers immediately float small defects, fill small holes and apply curing.","Core walls will be covered by finishes later, so curing slipformed surfaces does not matter.","A core passes acceptance if its total height and overall verticality are within tolerance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"混凝土出模時表面仍很年輕，懸吊在平台下方的修飾架讓工人可以立即抹平小缺陷、填補小孔洞，並施加養護。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Concrete leaving the form is very young, and finishing scaffolds hung below the deck let workers immediately float small defects, fill small holes and apply curing. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b061-v13-34","title":"出模後修飾、養護與耐久：定量估算","titleEn":"Finishing, curing and durability after exit: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「出模面修飾與養護」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Exit-surface finishing and curing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：蒸發率 E = 5[(T_c+18)^2.5 − r(T_a+18)^2.5](V+4)×10⁻⁶（kg/m²/h）。混凝土與氣溫 25°C、相對濕度 r = 0.4、風速 29 km/h（約 8 m/s）時 E = 5×(12,124 − 4,850)×33×10⁻⁶ ≈ 1.2 kg/m²/h，超過常用的 1.0 kg/m²/h 警戒值，需要養護劑或圍幕防風。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Evaporation rate E = 5[(T_c+18)^2.5 − r(T_a+18)^2.5](V+4)×10⁻⁶ in kg/m²/h. With concrete and air at 25°C, r = 0.4 and wind 29 km/h (about 8 m/s), E = 5×(12,124 − 4,850)×33×10⁻⁶ ≈ 1.2 kg/m²/h, above the common 1.0 kg/m²/h caution level, so curing compound or wind screens are needed. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在平台高度設風速計與溫濕度計，每班計算蒸發率並記錄養護措施；定期以回彈錘或表面吸水試驗比較不同高程的表層品質，發現粉化或裂縫時檢討養護方式。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Install an anemometer and temperature–humidity sensor at deck level, compute evaporation each shift and log curing measures; compare surface quality at different heights periodically with a rebound hammer or surface absorption tests, and revise curing when dusting or cracking appears.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"蒸發率 E = 5[(T_c+18)^2.5 − r(T_a+18)^2.5](V+4)×10⁻⁶（kg/m²/h）。混凝土與氣溫 25°C、相對濕度 r = 0.4、風速 29 km/h（約 8 m/s）時 E = 5×(12,124 − 4,850)×33×10⁻⁶ ≈ 1.2 kg/m²/h，超過常用的 1.0 kg/m²/h 警戒值，需要養護劑或圍幕防風。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Evaporation rate E = 5[(T_c+18)^2.5 − r(T_a+18)^2.5](V+4)×10⁻⁶ in kg/m²/h. With concrete and air at 25°C, r = 0.4 and wind 29 km/h (about 8 m/s), E = 5×(12,124 − 4,850)×33×10⁻⁶ ≈ 1.2 kg/m²/h, above the common 1.0 kg/m²/h caution level, so curing compound or wind screens are needed. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「出模後修飾、養護與耐久」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Finishing, curing and durability after exit\", which statement holds?","options":["滑模的速度越快越好，只要千斤頂能力足夠就可以一直加速。","蒸發率 E = 5[(T_c+18)^2.5 − r(T_a+18)^2.5](V+4)×10⁻⁶（kg/m²/h）。","滑模速度快，所以埋件位置可以完工後再用鑽孔方式補做。"],"optionsEn":["The faster the slipform the better; it can keep accelerating as long as the jacks are strong enough.","Evaporation rate E = 5[(T_c+18)^2.5 − r(T_a+18)^2.5](V+4)×10⁻⁶ in kg/m²/h.","Because slipforming is fast, embed positions can be added afterwards by drilling."],"answer":1,"explanation":"蒸發率 E = 5[(T_c+18)^2.5 − r(T_a+18)^2.5](V+4)×10⁻⁶（kg/m²/h）。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Evaporation rate E = 5[(T_c+18)^2.5 − r(T_a+18)^2.5](V+4)×10⁻⁶ in kg/m²/h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b061-v13-35","title":"出模後修飾、養護與耐久：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Finishing, curing and durability after exit: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「出模面修飾與養護」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Exit-surface finishing and curing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在平台高度設風速計與溫濕度計，每班計算蒸發率並記錄養護措施；定期以回彈錘或表面吸水試驗比較不同高程的表層品質，發現粉化或裂縫時檢討養護方式。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Install an anemometer and temperature–humidity sensor at deck level, compute evaporation each shift and log curing measures; compare surface quality at different heights periodically with a rebound hammer or surface absorption tests, and revise curing when dusting or cracking appears. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：養護方法（養護劑、噴霧或圍幕）與適用風速條件要寫入施工計畫；修飾架的護欄、防墜網與緊急逃生路線在開滑前檢查，並在每次平台改裝後重新檢查。","observationEn":"Site practice: Write curing methods (compound, misting or screens) and the wind conditions for each into the method statement; inspect guardrails, fall-arrest nets and escape routes on the finishing scaffold before sliding starts and again after every deck modification.","failure":"注意干擾：強風下出模面只做抹平未養護，表面細密裂縫與粉化使保護層透水性升高，日後碳化與鋼筋鏽蝕提前；修飾架缺乏圍幕時，工人也暴露在高處強風與墜落風險下。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Floating the exit surface without curing in strong wind leaves fine cracks and dusting that make the cover more permeable, bringing forward carbonation and bar corrosion; finishing scaffolds without screens also expose workers to high wind and fall hazards. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在平台高度設風速計與溫濕度計，每班計算蒸發率並記錄養護措施；定期以回彈錘或表面吸水試驗比較不同高程的表層品質，發現粉化或裂縫時檢討養護方式。","textEn":"Install an anemometer and temperature–humidity sensor at deck level, compute evaporation each shift and log curing measures; compare surface quality at different heights periodically with a rebound hammer or surface absorption tests, and revise curing when dusting or cracking appears.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"養護方法（養護劑、噴霧或圍幕）與適用風速條件要寫入施工計畫；修飾架的護欄、防墜網與緊急逃生路線在開滑前檢查，並在每次平台改裝後重新檢查。","textEn":"Write curing methods (compound, misting or screens) and the wind conditions for each into the method statement; inspect guardrails, fall-arrest nets and escape routes on the finishing scaffold before sliding starts and again after every deck modification.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「出模後修飾、養護與耐久」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Finishing, curing and durability after exit\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","滑模混凝土是連續澆置的，所以牆內不會有施工縫。","在平台高度設風速計與溫濕度計，每班計算蒸發率並記錄養護措施；定期以回彈錘或表面吸水試驗比較不同高程的表層品質，發現粉化或裂縫時檢討養護方式。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Slipformed walls are cast continuously, so they never contain construction joints.","Install an anemometer and temperature–humidity sensor at deck level, compute evaporation each shift and log curing measures."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在平台高度設風速計與溫濕度計，每班計算蒸發率並記錄養護措施；定期以回彈錘或表面吸水試驗比較不同高程的表層品質，發現粉化或裂縫時檢討養護方式。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Install an anemometer and temperature–humidity sensor at deck level, compute evaporation each shift and log curing measures; compare surface quality at different heights periodically with a rebound hammer or surface absorption tests, and revise curing when dusting or cracking appears. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b061-v13-36","title":"出模後修飾、養護與耐久：失效診斷","titleEn":"Finishing, curing and durability after exit: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「出模面修飾與養護」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Exit-surface finishing and curing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"強風下出模面只做抹平未養護，表面細密裂縫與粉化使保護層透水性升高，日後碳化與鋼筋鏽蝕提前；修飾架缺乏圍幕時，工人也暴露在高處強風與墜落風險下。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Floating the exit surface without curing in strong wind leaves fine cracks and dusting that make the cover more permeable, bringing forward carbonation and bar corrosion; finishing scaffolds without screens also expose workers to high wind and fall hazards. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：修飾架也是人員作業區，需要護欄與防墜網。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The finishing scaffold is also a work area that needs guardrails and fall-arrest netting.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「核心筒以後會被裝修包覆，所以滑模牆面的養護不重要。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Core walls will be covered by finishes later, so curing slipformed surfaces does not matter.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"強風下出模面只做抹平未養護，表面細密裂縫與粉化使保護層透水性升高，日後碳化與鋼筋鏽蝕提前；修飾架缺乏圍幕時，工人也暴露在高處強風與墜落風險下。","textEn":"Floating the exit surface without curing in strong wind leaves fine cracks and dusting that make the cover more permeable, bringing forward carbonation and bar corrosion; finishing scaffolds without screens also expose workers to high wind and fall hazards.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「出模後修飾、養護與耐久」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Finishing, curing and durability after exit\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["強風下出模面只做抹平未養護，表面細密裂縫與粉化使保護層透水性升高，日後碳化與鋼筋鏽蝕提前；修飾架缺乏圍幕時，工人也暴露在高處強風與墜落風險下。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","核心筒驗收只要總高度與整體垂直度合格就足夠。"],"optionsEn":["Floating the exit surface without curing in strong wind leaves fine cracks and dusting that make the cover more permeable, bringing forward carbonation and bar corrosion.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A core passes acceptance if its total height and overall verticality are within tolerance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"強風下出模面只做抹平未養護，表面細密裂縫與粉化使保護層透水性升高，日後碳化與鋼筋鏽蝕提前；修飾架缺乏圍幕時，工人也暴露在高處強風與墜落風險下。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Floating the exit surface without curing in strong wind leaves fine cracks and dusting that make the cover more permeable, bringing forward carbonation and bar corrosion; finishing scaffolds without screens also expose workers to high wind and fall hazards. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b061-v13-37","title":"竣工量測、偏差統計與工程交接：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"As-built survey, deviation statistics and handover: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「竣工偏差與交接紀錄」如何影響高層建築核心筒滑模施工的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “As-built deviation and handover records” governs force, deformation or durability in “Slipform construction of high-rise cores”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"滑模核心筒完成後，後續的樓板、鋼梁、電梯導軌與帷幕牆都以核心筒為基準，所以核心筒的實際位置比設計位置更重要。竣工量測要提供每一高程的牆面位置、垂直度、扭轉、開口與埋件實際座標，讓後續工種調整連接。羅特魏爾試驗塔直徑約 21 m、內含 12 個井道，殼體高約 232 m，井道的垂直度直接決定電梯試驗能否進行。交接資料還應包括冷縫位置、修補紀錄與強度試驗結果，作為日後鑽孔、補強或變更用途的依據。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「竣工偏差與交接紀錄」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Once a slipformed core is complete, floors, steel beams, elevator rails and the façade all reference it, so the core's actual position matters more than its design position. The as-built survey must give wall position, verticality, twist and the actual coordinates of openings and embeds at each level so following trades can adjust their connections. The Rottweil test tower, about 21 m in diameter with 12 shafts and a shell about 232 m tall, shows how shaft verticality decides whether elevator testing can proceed at all. Handover records should also include cold-joint locations, repair records and strength results, as the basis for later drilling, strengthening or change of use. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “As-built deviation and handover records” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：40 個測點的垂直偏差平均 4 mm、標準差 3 mm，95% 上界 ≈ 4 + 1.96×3 ≈ 9.9 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Forty survey points with a mean verticality deviation of 4 mm and standard deviation 3 mm give a 95% upper bound of about 4 + 1.96×3 ≈ 9.9 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「核心筒驗收只要總高度與整體垂直度合格就足夠。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A core passes acceptance if its total height and overall verticality are within tolerance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「竣工偏差與交接紀錄」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “As-built deviation and handover records”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-37-k1","title":"竣工量測、偏差統計與工程交接","titleEn":"As-built survey, deviation statistics and handover","text":"滑模核心筒完成後，後續的樓板、鋼梁、電梯導軌與帷幕牆都以核心筒為基準，所以核心筒的實際位置比設計位置更重要。竣工量測要提供每一高程的牆面位置、垂直度、扭轉、開口與埋件實際座標，讓後續工種調整連接。","textEn":"Once a slipformed core is complete, floors, steel beams, elevator rails and the façade all reference it, so the core's actual position matters more than its design position. The as-built survey must give wall position, verticality, twist and the actual coordinates of openings and embeds at each level so following trades can adjust their connections.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：核心筒驗收只要總高度與整體垂直度合格就足夠。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A core passes acceptance if its total height and overall verticality are within tolerance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「竣工量測、偏差統計與工程交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"As-built survey, deviation statistics and handover\" is correct?","options":["核心筒驗收只要總高度與整體垂直度合格就足夠。","滑模核心筒完成後，後續的樓板、鋼梁、電梯導軌與帷幕牆都以核心筒為基準，所以核心筒的實際位置比設計位置更重要。","滑模適用於所有高層核心筒，只要速度夠快就一定比較省工期。"],"optionsEn":["A core passes acceptance if its total height and overall verticality are within tolerance.","Once a slipformed core is complete, floors, steel beams, elevator rails and the façade all reference it, so the core's actual position matters more than its design position.","Slipforming suits every high-rise core and is always faster if the rate is high enough."],"answer":1,"explanation":"滑模核心筒完成後，後續的樓板、鋼梁、電梯導軌與帷幕牆都以核心筒為基準，所以核心筒的實際位置比設計位置更重要。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Once a slipformed core is complete, floors, steel beams, elevator rails and the façade all reference it, so the core's actual position matters more than its design position. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b061-v13-38","title":"竣工量測、偏差統計與工程交接：定量估算","titleEn":"As-built survey, deviation statistics and handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「竣工偏差與交接紀錄」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “As-built deviation and handover records” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：40 個測點的垂直偏差平均 4 mm、標準差 3 mm，95% 上界 ≈ 4 + 1.96×3 ≈ 9.9 mm。以 ACI 117 對高度超過約 25 m 者取高度 1/1,000、上限約 150 mm 的概念，120 m 核心筒容許約 120 mm，實測遠在容許內；但電梯導軌要求常更嚴，須另行比對。數值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Forty survey points with a mean verticality deviation of 4 mm and standard deviation 3 mm give a 95% upper bound of about 4 + 1.96×3 ≈ 9.9 mm. Using the ACI 117 concept of 1/1,000 of height for heights above about 25 m, capped at about 150 mm, a 120 m core is allowed about 120 mm, so the result is well within; elevator rail requirements are often stricter and must be checked separately. Values are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：竣工量測以獨立於施工測量的控制點進行，結果與滑升日誌中的每班量測比對，差異需可解釋；電梯井道另以雷射掃描或吊線量測淨尺寸，交給電梯廠商確認導軌安裝可行。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Carry out the as-built survey from control points independent of the construction survey, compare it with the shift readings in the slip log and explain any differences; survey elevator shaft clear dimensions separately by laser scanning or plumb lines and give them to the elevator supplier to confirm rail installation is feasible.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"40 個測點的垂直偏差平均 4 mm、標準差 3 mm，95% 上界 ≈ 4 + 1.96×3 ≈ 9.9 mm。以 ACI 117 對高度超過約 25 m 者取高度 1/1,000、上限約 150 mm 的概念，120 m 核心筒容許約 120 mm，實測遠在容許內；但電梯導軌要求常更嚴，須另行比對。數值為教學假設。","textEn":"Forty survey points with a mean verticality deviation of 4 mm and standard deviation 3 mm give a 95% upper bound of about 4 + 1.96×3 ≈ 9.9 mm. Using the ACI 117 concept of 1/1,000 of height for heights above about 25 m, capped at about 150 mm, a 120 m core is allowed about 120 mm, so the result is well within; elevator rail requirements are often stricter and must be checked separately. Values are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「竣工量測、偏差統計與工程交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"As-built survey, deviation statistics and handover\", which statement holds?","options":["千斤頂額定荷重夠大，就代表爬桿與平台一定安全。","滑模偏了只要在下一段一次調回原位即可。","40 個測點的垂直偏差平均 4 mm、標準差 3 mm，95% 上界 ≈ 4 + 1.96×3 ≈ 9.9 mm。"],"optionsEn":["If the jack rating is high enough, the rods and deck must be safe.","If the slipform drifts, it can simply be returned to position in the next lift.","Forty survey points with a mean verticality deviation of 4 mm and standard deviation 3 mm give a 95% upper bound of about 4 + 1.96×3 ≈ 9.9 mm."],"answer":2,"explanation":"40 個測點的垂直偏差平均 4 mm、標準差 3 mm，95% 上界 ≈ 4 + 1.96×3 ≈ 9.9 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Forty survey points with a mean verticality deviation of 4 mm and standard deviation 3 mm give a 95% upper bound of about 4 + 1.96×3 ≈ 9.9 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b061-v13-39","title":"竣工量測、偏差統計與工程交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"As-built survey, deviation statistics and handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「竣工偏差與交接紀錄」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “As-built deviation and handover records” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"竣工量測以獨立於施工測量的控制點進行，結果與滑升日誌中的每班量測比對，差異需可解釋；電梯井道另以雷射掃描或吊線量測淨尺寸，交給電梯廠商確認導軌安裝可行。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Carry out the as-built survey from control points independent of the construction survey, compare it with the shift readings in the slip log and explain any differences; survey elevator shaft clear dimensions separately by laser scanning or plumb lines and give them to the elevator supplier to confirm rail installation is feasible. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接文件應包含按高程排列的竣工座標表、埋件與開口實測表、冷縫與修補位置圖、強度試驗彙整與滑升日誌；任何日後在核心筒上鑽孔或開口，都須先查閱這些資料並經結構工程師核准。","observationEn":"Site practice: Handover should include elevation-ordered as-built coordinate tables, measured embed and opening tables, maps of cold joints and repairs, strength-test summaries and the slip log; any future drilling or opening in the core must consult these records and be approved by a structural engineer.","failure":"注意干擾：竣工資料只交一張總體垂直度數字，後續鋼梁廠商依設計座標製作，到現場才發現埋件偏移，大量現場修改；冷縫與修補位置未記錄，多年後在冷縫處鑽孔或開口，削弱牆體剪力傳遞。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Handing over only a single overall verticality figure leads steel fabricators to work to design coordinates and find displaced embeds on site, forcing extensive field modifications; with cold joints and repairs unrecorded, someone later drills or cuts openings at a cold joint and weakens shear transfer. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"竣工量測以獨立於施工測量的控制點進行，結果與滑升日誌中的每班量測比對，差異需可解釋；電梯井道另以雷射掃描或吊線量測淨尺寸，交給電梯廠商確認導軌安裝可行。","textEn":"Carry out the as-built survey from control points independent of the construction survey, compare it with the shift readings in the slip log and explain any differences; survey elevator shaft clear dimensions separately by laser scanning or plumb lines and give them to the elevator supplier to confirm rail installation is feasible.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接文件應包含按高程排列的竣工座標表、埋件與開口實測表、冷縫與修補位置圖、強度試驗彙整與滑升日誌；任何日後在核心筒上鑽孔或開口，都須先查閱這些資料並經結構工程師核准。","textEn":"Handover should include elevation-ordered as-built coordinate tables, measured embed and opening tables, maps of cold joints and repairs, strength-test summaries and the slip log; any future drilling or opening in the core must consult these records and be approved by a structural engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「竣工量測、偏差統計與工程交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"As-built survey, deviation statistics and handover\"?","options":["竣工量測以獨立於施工測量的控制點進行，結果與滑升日誌中的每班量測比對，差異需可解釋；電梯井道另以雷射掃描或吊線量測淨尺寸，交給電梯廠商確認導軌安裝可行。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","混凝土在模板內放滿固定小時數就一定可以出模，與溫度無關。"],"optionsEn":["Carry out the as-built survey from control points independent of the construction survey, compare it with the shift readings in the slip log and explain any differences.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Concrete can always leave the form after a fixed number of hours regardless of temperature."],"answer":0,"explanation":"竣工量測以獨立於施工測量的控制點進行，結果與滑升日誌中的每班量測比對，差異需可解釋；電梯井道另以雷射掃描或吊線量測淨尺寸，交給電梯廠商確認導軌安裝可行。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Carry out the as-built survey from control points independent of the construction survey, compare it with the shift readings in the slip log and explain any differences; survey elevator shaft clear dimensions separately by laser scanning or plumb lines and give them to the elevator supplier to confirm rail installation is feasible. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b061-v13-40","title":"竣工量測、偏差統計與工程交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"As-built survey, deviation statistics and handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"prerequisiteIds":["b061-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「竣工偏差與交接紀錄」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “As-built deviation and handover records” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"竣工資料只交一張總體垂直度數字，後續鋼梁廠商依設計座標製作，到現場才發現埋件偏移，大量現場修改；冷縫與修補位置未記錄，多年後在冷縫處鑽孔或開口，削弱牆體剪力傳遞。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Handing over only a single overall verticality figure leads steel fabricators to work to design coordinates and find displaced embeds on site, forcing extensive field modifications; with cold joints and repairs unrecorded, someone later drills or cuts openings at a cold joint and weakens shear transfer. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：交接資料還應包括冷縫位置、修補紀錄與強度試驗結果，作為日後鑽孔、補強或變更用途的依據。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Handover records should also include cold-joint locations, repair records and strength results, as the basis for later drilling, strengthening or change of use.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「核心筒驗收只要總高度與整體垂直度合格就足夠。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A core passes acceptance if its total height and overall verticality are within tolerance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b061-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"竣工資料只交一張總體垂直度數字，後續鋼梁廠商依設計座標製作，到現場才發現埋件偏移，大量現場修改；冷縫與修補位置未記錄，多年後在冷縫處鑽孔或開口，削弱牆體剪力傳遞。","textEn":"Handing over only a single overall verticality figure leads steel fabricators to work to design coordinates and find displaced embeds on site, forcing extensive field modifications; with cold joints and repairs unrecorded, someone later drills or cuts openings at a cold joint and weakens shear transfer.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]},{"id":"b061-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「竣工量測、偏差統計與工程交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"As-built survey, deviation statistics and handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","竣工資料只交一張總體垂直度數字，後續鋼梁廠商依設計座標製作，到現場才發現埋件偏移，大量現場修改。","滑模適用於所有高層核心筒，只要速度夠快就一定比較省工期。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Handing over only a single overall verticality figure leads steel fabricators to work to design coordinates and find displaced embeds on site, forcing extensive field modifications.","Slipforming suits every high-rise core and is always faster if the rate is high enough."],"answer":1,"explanation":"竣工資料只交一張總體垂直度數字，後續鋼梁廠商依設計座標製作，到現場才發現埋件偏移，大量現場修改；冷縫與修補位置未記錄，多年後在冷縫處鑽孔或開口，削弱牆體剪力傳遞。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Handing over only a single overall verticality figure leads steel fabricators to work to design coordinates and find displaced embeds on site, forcing extensive field modifications; with cold joints and repairs unrecorded, someone later drills or cuts openings at a cold joint and weakens shear transfer. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-cn-tower-history","v13s-tke-atlanta-tower-release","v13s-enr-atlanta-slipform","v13s-zueblin-rottweil","v13s-osha-1926-703"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
